PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L12U6.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":12,"cefr":"C2","unit":6,"theme":"Legacy","essential_question":"What will we leave behind for the generations who come after us?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS1","title":"Has Shaped, Has Been Teaching, Is Being Modest: Aspect for Stance and Relevance","objectives":["Students will be able to choose between the past simple and the present perfect (simple or continuous) to signal finished or ongoing relevance.","Students will be able to use continuous aspect for temporary behavior and stative verbs with dynamic meanings.","I can explain the difference between \"Al-Fihri founded the university\" and \"The university has been teaching students for eleven centuries.\"","I can say \"He's being modest\" about temporary behavior."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من الاختيار بين الماضي البسيط والمضارع التام (البسيط أو المستمر) للدلالة على الانتهاء أو الصلة المستمرة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام الصيغة المستمرة للسلوك المؤقت والأفعال الحالية بمعانٍ حركية.","أستطيع أن أشرح الفرق بين Al-Fihri founded the university وThe university has been teaching students for eleven centuries.","أستطيع أن أقول He's being modest عن سلوك مؤقت."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"pioneer","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌpaɪəˈnɪr/","definition":"one of the first people to do something new","arabic":"رائد","example":"Ibn Sina was a pioneer of modern medicine.","image_id":"GV-L12-U6-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS1-W01"},{"word":"enduring","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ɛndˈjʊrɪŋ/","definition":"lasting for a long time","arabic":"دائم / باقٍ","example":"Her poems have had an enduring influence.","image_id":"GV-L12-U6-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS1-W02"},{"word":"trailblazer","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtreɪlˌbleɪzɚ/","definition":"a person who is the first to do something and shows others the way","arabic":"رائد يشقّ الطريق","example":"She was a trailblazer for women in science.","image_id":"GV-L12-U6-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS1-W03"},{"word":"posterity","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pɑˈstɛrəti/","definition":"all the people who will live in the future","arabic":"الأجيال القادمة","example":"The letters were preserved for posterity.","image_id":"GV-L12-U6-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Past simple presents an event as finished and separate from now: Al-Fihri founded the university in 859. Present perfect connects the past to the present – the result or influence still matters: The idea has outlived its creator. Al-Khwarizmi has influenced modern life. A writer can use this choice to show stance: \"Ibn Sina was a great doctor\" (history) vs \"Ibn Sina has shaped medicine\" (still relevant).\nPresent perfect continuous stresses duration or an ongoing / recent activity: The university has been teaching students for eleven centuries. Historians have been reassessing his work. Past perfect sets up background in a narrative: She had inherited a fortune before she founded the university. Use the present simple to report the current views of sources: Many historians argue that…\nContinuous forms show something temporary, in progress or changing: We are relying on his ideas right now. English is becoming a global language. With always, they can show annoyance: He is always interrupting. be being + adjective = temporary behavior: You're being modest. (Usually you're not.) Some stative verbs have dynamic meanings: I think it's true (opinion) / I'm thinking about my future (considering); She has a library (possess) / She's having lunch (experience).\npast simple = finished past • present perfect = past with present relevance\npresent perfect continuous = duration / ongoing influence\npast perfect = earlier background in a narrative • present simple = current stance of sources\ncontinuous = temporary, in progress, changing, annoying (always) • be being + adjective","examples":["The idea has outlived its creator by centuries.","Fatima al-Fihri founded al-Qarawiyyin in 859.","The university has been teaching students for eleven centuries.","She had inherited a fortune before she founded it.","Every time we search online, we are relying on his ideas.","Many historians argue that the \"Canon\" shaped European medicine.","You're being modest – your project was excellent.","I'm thinking about what legacy I want to leave."],"common_errors":["✗ Fatima al-Fihri has founded al-Qarawiyyin in 859. → ✓ Fatima al-Fihri founded al-Qarawiyyin in 859. (Finished time (859) → past simple.)","✗ The university teaches students since 859. → ✓ The university has been teaching students since 859. (since → present perfect (continuous).)","✗ I am thinking that his ideas are important. (opinion) → ✓ I think that his ideas are important. (Opinion → stative think.)","✗ He is modest today; usually he boasts. → ✓ He is being modest today. (Temporary behavior → be being.)"],"arabic":"الماضي البسيط يعرض الحدث منتهيًا: Al-Fihri founded the university in 859، والمضارع التام يربط الماضي بالحاضر لأن الأثر ما زال قائمًا: The idea has outlived its creator.\nالمضارع التام المستمر يؤكد المدة أو الأثر المستمر: The university has been teaching students for eleven centuries، والماضي التام للخلفية في السرد.\nنستخدم المضارع البسيط لعرض موقف المصادر الحالي: Many historians argue that…\nالصيغة المستمرة للمؤقت والمتغير والمزعج (always)، وbe being + صفة للسلوك المؤقت، وبعض الأفعال الحالية لها معنى حركي: I'm thinking about my future."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Has Shaped, Has Been Teaching, Is Being Modest: Aspect for Stance and Relevance”. Let’s learn choosing aspect to show stance: present perfect for present relevance or ongoing influence (has outlived, has shaped) vs past simple for a finished past (founded, wrote); present perfect continuous for ongoing or recent activity and duration (has been teaching, have been reassessing); past perfect for background events in narratives (had inherited); present continuous for temporary situations, trends and annoying habits (is becoming, is always complaining); be being + adjective for temporary behavior (He's being modest); stative verbs with dynamic meanings (I'm thinking of…, She's having lunch); present simple for the current stance of sources (Historians argue…) together.","on_screen":"GV-L12-U6-LS1 | Has Shaped, Has Been Teaching, Is Being Modest: Aspect for Stance and Relevance","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Lives That Outlast Us”: What does it mean to leave a legacy? For some, it is a building or a fortune; for others, it is an idea that has outlived its creator by centuries. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"What does it mean to leave a legacy? For some, it is a building or a fortune; for others, it is an idea that has outlived its creator by centuries.","visual":"Image GV-L12-U6-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Past simple presents an event as finished and separate from now: Al-Fihri founded the university in 859. Present perfect connects the past to the present – the result or influence still matters: The idea has outlived its creator. Al-Khwarizmi has influenced modern life. A writer can use this choice to show stance: \"Ibn Sina was a great doctor\" (history) vs \"Ibn Sina has shaped medicine\" (still relevant). Present perfect continuous stresses duration or an ongoing / recent activity: The university has been teaching students for eleven centuries. Historians have been reassessing his work. Past perfect sets up background in a narrative: She had inherited a fortune before she founded the university. Use the present simple to report the current views of sources: Many historians argue that…","on_screen":"past simple = finished past • present perfect = past with present relevance • present perfect continuous = duration / ongoing influence • past perfect = earlier background in a narrative • present simple = current stance of sources","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The idea has outlived its creator by centuries. Fatima al-Fihri founded al-Qarawiyyin in 859. The university has been teaching students for eleven centuries.","on_screen":"The idea has outlived its creator by centuries. / Fatima al-Fihri founded al-Qarawiyyin in 859. / The university has been teaching students for eleven centuries.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Fatima al-Fihri has founded al-Qarawiyyin in 859.” That’s not right. We say: “Fatima al-Fihri founded al-Qarawiyyin in 859.” Finished time (859) → past simple.","on_screen":"✗ Fatima al-Fihri has founded al-Qarawiyyin in 859.   ✓ Fatima al-Fihri founded al-Qarawiyyin in 859.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:15","narration":"Quick check: \"Fatima al-Fihri founded al-Qarawiyyin in 859.\" Why past simple? … Think! … A finished time in the past (859). Great job! Now you can say: I can explain the difference between \"Al-Fihri founded the university\" and \"The university has been teaching students for eleven centuries.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can explain the difference between \"Al-Fihri founded the university\" and \"The university has been teaching students for eleven centuries.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: choosing aspect to show stance: present perfect for present relevance or ongoing influence (has outlived, has shaped) vs past simple for a finished past (founded, wrote); present perfect continuous for ongoing or recent activity and duration (has been teaching, have been reassessing); past perfect for background events in narratives (had inherited); present continuous for temporary situations, trends and annoying habits (is becoming, is always complaining); be being + adjective for temporary behavior (He's being modest); stative verbs with dynamic meanings (I'm thinking of…, She's having lunch); present simple for the current stance of sources (Historians argue…).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الماضي البسيط يعرض الحدث منتهيًا: Al-Fihri founded the university in 859، والمضارع التام يربط الماضي بالحاضر لأن الأثر ما زال قائمًا: The idea has outlived its creator.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Fatima al-Fihri has founded al-Qarawiyyin in 859. — الصحيح: Fatima al-Fihri founded al-Qarawiyyin in 859.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أشرح الفرق بين Al-Fihri founded the university وThe university has been teaching students for eleven centuries."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Lives That Outlast Us","body":"What does it mean to leave a legacy? For some, it is a building or a fortune; for others, it is an idea that has outlived its creator by centuries.\nIn 859, Fatima al-Fihri founded al-Qarawiyyin in the Moroccan city of Fez. The institution has been teaching students for more than eleven centuries, and many regard it as the oldest continuously operating university in the world. Al-Fihri had inherited a fortune from her father; rather than spending it on herself, she invested it in learning.\nThe ninth-century mathematician al-Khwarizmi has arguably influenced modern life more than any ruler of his age. The word \"algebra\" comes from the title of his most famous book, and the word \"algorithm\" is derived from his name. Every time we use a search engine, we are relying on ideas that he helped to develop.\nIbn Sina's \"Canon of Medicine\" was studied in European universities for centuries. In recent decades, historians have been reassessing its influence, and many now argue that it shaped medical education far beyond the Islamic world.\nLegacies are not only for famous people, however. A grandmother who has been telling the same stories to three generations, a teacher whose former students are now teaching others, a volunteer who has planted trees that will shade people she will never meet: each of them is building something that will last.\nThe question, then, is not whether we will leave a legacy, but what kind. We are writing ours every day.","word_count":246,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Fatima al-Fihri ___ al-Qarawiyyin in the year 859.","options":["founded","has founded","had been founding","has been founding"],"answer":"founded","explanation":"Past simple vs present perfect (relevance).","explanation_ar":"الماضي أم التام."},{"q":"The institution ___ students for more than eleven centuries.","options":["was teaching","taught","teaches since","has been teaching"],"answer":"has been teaching","explanation":"Present perfect continuous (duration, ongoing).","explanation_ar":"التام المستمر."},{"q":"Al-Fihri ___ a fortune from her father before she founded the university.","options":["inherits","was inheriting","had inherited","has inherited"],"answer":"had inherited","explanation":"Past perfect for background.","explanation_ar":"الماضي التام."},{"q":"Every time we use a search engine, we ___ on ideas that al-Khwarizmi helped to develop.","options":["had relied","relied","have relied since","are relying"],"answer":"are relying","explanation":"Continuous for temporary, changing or annoying.","explanation_ar":"الصيغة المستمرة."},{"q":"You ___ modest; your project was the best in the class.","options":["are","are being","be","have been being"],"answer":"are being","explanation":"Stative vs dynamic meaning; be being.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال الحالية."},{"q":"In recent decades, historians ______ the influence of Ibn Sina's \"Canon of Medicine,\" and many now argue that it shaped medical education far beyond the Islamic world.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["have been reassessing","are reassess","had been reassessing tomorrow","reassessed in"],"answer":"have been reassessing","explanation":"Present perfect continuous (duration, ongoing).","explanation_ar":"التام المستمر."}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the best tense or aspect. Word bank: argue, wrote, has been telling","items":[{"q":"My grandmother ______ (tell) the same stories to three generations.","options":[],"answer":"has been telling","explanation":"Present perfect continuous (duration, ongoing).","explanation_ar":"التام المستمر."},{"q":"Al-Khwarizmi ______ (write) his famous book on algebra in the ninth century.","options":[],"answer":"wrote","explanation":"Past simple vs present perfect (relevance).","explanation_ar":"الماضي أم التام."},{"q":"Many historians ______ (argue) that his work changed mathematics forever.","options":[],"answer":"argue","explanation":"Present simple for the stance of sources.","explanation_ar":"موقف المصادر."}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"Ibn Sina has written the \"Canon of Medicine\" in the eleventh century.","options":[],"answer":"Ibn Sina wrote the \"Canon of Medicine\" in the eleventh century.","explanation":"has written → wrote. Past simple vs present perfect (relevance).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: has written → wrote. الماضي أم التام."},{"q":"The library collects manuscripts since 1950.","options":[],"answer":"The library has been collecting manuscripts since 1950.","explanation":"collects → has been collecting. Present perfect continuous (duration, ongoing).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: collects → has been collecting. التام المستمر."},{"q":"I am thinking that his ideas are still important today. (opinion)","options":[],"answer":"I think that his ideas are still important today. (opinion)","explanation":"am thinking → think. Stative vs dynamic meaning; be being.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: am thinking → think. الأفعال الحالية."}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Show relevance and stance.","items":[{"q":"Write about a historical person's finished action (past simple) and their lasting influence (present perfect).","options":[],"answer":"Al-Khwarizmi wrote a book on algebra; his ideas have shaped modern computing.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses choosing aspect to show stance: present perfect for present relevance or ongoing influence (has outlived, has shaped) vs past simple for a finished past (founded, wrote); present perfect continuous for ongoing or recent activity and duration (has been teaching, have been reassessing); past perfect for background events in narratives (had inherited); present continuous for temporary situations, trends and annoying habits (is becoming, is always complaining); be being + adjective for temporary behavior (He's being modest); stative verbs with dynamic meanings (I'm thinking of…, She's having lunch); present simple for the current stance of sources (Historians argue…) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write about something that has been going on for a long time.","options":[],"answer":"My father has been reading the same newspaper every morning for thirty years.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses choosing aspect to show stance: present perfect for present relevance or ongoing influence (has outlived, has shaped) vs past simple for a finished past (founded, wrote); present perfect continuous for ongoing or recent activity and duration (has been teaching, have been reassessing); past perfect for background events in narratives (had inherited); present continuous for temporary situations, trends and annoying habits (is becoming, is always complaining); be being + adjective for temporary behavior (He's being modest); stative verbs with dynamic meanings (I'm thinking of…, She's having lunch); present simple for the current stance of sources (Historians argue…) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a narrative sentence with past perfect background.","options":[],"answer":"By the time the museum opened, the volunteers had restored every manuscript.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses choosing aspect to show stance: present perfect for present relevance or ongoing influence (has outlived, has shaped) vs past simple for a finished past (founded, wrote); present perfect continuous for ongoing or recent activity and duration (has been teaching, have been reassessing); past perfect for background events in narratives (had inherited); present continuous for temporary situations, trends and annoying habits (is becoming, is always complaining); be being + adjective for temporary behavior (He's being modest); stative verbs with dynamic meanings (I'm thinking of…, She's having lunch); present simple for the current stance of sources (Historians argue…) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Describe someone's temporary behavior with \"be being\".","options":[],"answer":"My little brother is being very helpful today; he must want something.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses choosing aspect to show stance: present perfect for present relevance or ongoing influence (has outlived, has shaped) vs past simple for a finished past (founded, wrote); present perfect continuous for ongoing or recent activity and duration (has been teaching, have been reassessing); past perfect for background events in narratives (had inherited); present continuous for temporary situations, trends and annoying habits (is becoming, is always complaining); be being + adjective for temporary behavior (He's being modest); stative verbs with dynamic meanings (I'm thinking of…, She's having lunch); present simple for the current stance of sources (Historians argue…) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Report a current view with \"experts / historians argue that…\".","options":[],"answer":"Historians argue that the old trade routes shaped Arabian culture.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses choosing aspect to show stance: present perfect for present relevance or ongoing influence (has outlived, has shaped) vs past simple for a finished past (founded, wrote); present perfect continuous for ongoing or recent activity and duration (has been teaching, have been reassessing); past perfect for background events in narratives (had inherited); present continuous for temporary situations, trends and annoying habits (is becoming, is always complaining); be being + adjective for temporary behavior (He's being modest); stative verbs with dynamic meanings (I'm thinking of…, She's having lunch); present simple for the current stance of sources (Historians argue…) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: A short biography.","items":[{"q":"Write 2 sentences about a person who has influenced your community, mixing past simple and present perfect.","options":[],"answer":"My grandfather opened the first bookshop in our town in 1975. He has inspired many young people to read.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses choosing aspect to show stance: present perfect for present relevance or ongoing influence (has outlived, has shaped) vs past simple for a finished past (founded, wrote); present perfect continuous for ongoing or recent activity and duration (has been teaching, have been reassessing); past perfect for background events in narratives (had inherited); present continuous for temporary situations, trends and annoying habits (is becoming, is always complaining); be being + adjective for temporary behavior (He's being modest); stative verbs with dynamic meanings (I'm thinking of…, She's having lunch); present simple for the current stance of sources (Historians argue…) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with the present perfect continuous about their ongoing influence.","options":[],"answer":"Since his retirement, he has been teaching children to write calligraphy.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses choosing aspect to show stance: present perfect for present relevance or ongoing influence (has outlived, has shaped) vs past simple for a finished past (founded, wrote); present perfect continuous for ongoing or recent activity and duration (has been teaching, have been reassessing); past perfect for background events in narratives (had inherited); present continuous for temporary situations, trends and annoying habits (is becoming, is always complaining); be being + adjective for temporary behavior (He's being modest); stative verbs with dynamic meanings (I'm thinking of…, She's having lunch); present simple for the current stance of sources (Historians argue…) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with a stative verb used dynamically.","options":[],"answer":"These days I am seeing my grandfather every weekend to learn from him.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses choosing aspect to show stance: present perfect for present relevance or ongoing influence (has outlived, has shaped) vs past simple for a finished past (founded, wrote); present perfect continuous for ongoing or recent activity and duration (has been teaching, have been reassessing); past perfect for background events in narratives (had inherited); present continuous for temporary situations, trends and annoying habits (is becoming, is always complaining); be being + adjective for temporary behavior (He's being modest); stative verbs with dynamic meanings (I'm thinking of…, She's having lunch); present simple for the current stance of sources (Historians argue…) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Ball Toss Sentences","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Students stand in a circle. The teacher says a cue word and throws the ball.","The catcher makes a sentence with the cue word and choosing aspect to show stance: present perfect for present relevance or ongoing influence (has outlived, has shaped) vs past simple for a finished past (founded, wrote); present perfect continuous for ongoing or recent activity and duration (has been teaching, have been reassessing); past perfect for background events in narratives (had inherited); present continuous for temporary situations, trends and annoying habits (is becoming, is always complaining); be being + adjective for temporary behavior (He's being modest); stative verbs with dynamic meanings (I'm thinking of…, She's having lunch); present simple for the current stance of sources (Historians argue…).","If it is correct, the catcher chooses the next cue word and throws the ball to a new student.","If it is not correct, classmates help fix it, and the same student tries again."],"data":[{"label":"has outlived"},{"label":"has been teaching"},{"label":"had inherited"},{"label":"are relying on"},{"label":"have been reassessing"},{"label":"historians argue"},{"label":"is being modest"},{"label":"We are writing ours"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The poet ___ in 1950, but his poems are still read today.","options":["died","had died since","has died","has been dying"],"answer":"died","explanation":"Past simple vs present perfect (relevance).","explanation_ar":"الماضي أم التام."},{"q":"His poems ___ readers for more than seventy years.","options":["inspire since","inspired","have been inspiring","were inspiring"],"answer":"have been inspiring","explanation":"Present perfect continuous (duration, ongoing).","explanation_ar":"التام المستمر."},{"q":"When the city built the new museum, the old library ___ for decades.","options":["has already closed","is already closing","had already closed","already closes"],"answer":"had already closed","explanation":"Past perfect for background.","explanation_ar":"الماضي التام."},{"q":"English ___ more important in international science every year.","options":["becomes since","has become since","became","is becoming"],"answer":"is becoming","explanation":"Continuous for temporary, changing or annoying.","explanation_ar":"الصيغة المستمرة."},{"q":"My cousin ___ interrupting me when I speak.","options":["is always","always is being","always has","has always been to"],"answer":"is always","explanation":"Continuous for temporary, changing or annoying.","explanation_ar":"الصيغة المستمرة."},{"q":"","options":["I'm having a big library at home.","I'm having lunch with my grandmother today.","I'm owning three old manuscripts.","I have lunch with my grandmother right now."],"answer":"I'm having lunch with my grandmother today.","explanation":"Stative vs dynamic meaning; be being.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال الحالية."},{"q":"","options":["Recent studies suggest that reading fiction can strengthen empathy.","Recent studies were suggest that reading fiction can strengthen empathy.","Recent studies have suggested yesterday that reading fiction can strengthen empathy.","Recent studies suggesting that reading fiction can strengthen empathy."],"answer":"Recent studies suggest that reading fiction can strengthen empathy.","explanation":"Present simple for the stance of sources.","explanation_ar":"موقف المصادر."},{"q":"Since its founding in the 1980s, the King Fahd National Library ______ hundreds of thousands of books and manuscripts for future generations.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["collects since","had collected tomorrow","collected in","has collected"],"answer":"has collected","explanation":"Past simple vs present perfect (relevance).","explanation_ar":"الماضي أم التام."},{"q":"By the time she founded the school, the young teacher ______ in three different countries and had learned four languages.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["lives","had lived","has lived","was living since"],"answer":"had lived","explanation":"Past perfect for background.","explanation_ar":"الماضي التام."},{"q":"Why does a writer choose \"Ibn Sina has shaped medicine\" instead of \"Ibn Sina shaped medicine\"?","options":["because the sentence is a question","because \"shaped\" is incorrect","to show that his influence is still relevant today","to show that his influence ended"],"answer":"to show that his influence is still relevant today","explanation":"Past simple vs present perfect (relevance).","explanation_ar":"الماضي أم التام."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"The courtyard of an ancient university in Fez with students reading under arches; a manuscript page of an algebra book; a family scene of a grandmother telling stories to children; a timeline from 859 to today. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"The courtyard of an ancient university in Fez with students reading under arches; a manuscript page of an algebra book; a family scene of a grandmother telling stories to children; a timeline from 859 to today"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about choosing aspect to show stance: present perfect for present relevance or ongoing influence (has outlived, has shaped) vs past simple for a finished past (founded, wrote); present perfect continuous for ongoing or recent activity and duration (has been teaching, have been reassessing); past perfect for background events in narratives (had inherited); present continuous for temporary situations, trends and annoying habits (is becoming, is always complaining); be being + adjective for temporary behavior (He's being modest); stative verbs with dynamic meanings (I'm thinking of…, She's having lunch); present simple for the current stance of sources (Historians argue…), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about choosing aspect to show stance: present perfect for present relevance or ongoing influence (has outlived, has shaped) vs past simple for a finished past (founded, wrote)"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows pioneer (one of the first people to do something new); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing pioneer: one of the first people to do something new"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows enduring (lasting for a long time); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing enduring: lasting for a long time"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows trailblazer (a person who is the first to do something and shows others the way); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing trailblazer: a person who is the first to do something and shows others the way"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows posterity (all the people who will live in the future); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing posterity: all the people who will live in the future"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Ball Toss Sentences”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Ball Toss Sentences"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS1-W01","script":"pioneer. pioneer. Ibn Sina was a pioneer of modern medicine.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS1-W02","script":"enduring. enduring. Her poems have had an enduring influence.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS1-W03","script":"trailblazer. trailblazer. She was a trailblazer for women in science.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS1-W04","script":"posterity. posterity. The letters were preserved for posterity.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS1-T1","script":"What does it mean to leave a legacy? For some, it is a building or a fortune; for others, it is an idea that has outlived its creator by centuries. In 859, Fatima al-Fihri founded al-Qarawiyyin in the Moroccan city of Fez. The institution has been teaching students for more than eleven centuries, and many regard it as the oldest continuously operating university in the world. Al-Fihri had inherited a fortune from her father; rather than spending it on herself, she invested it in learning. The ninth-century mathematician al-Khwarizmi has arguably influenced modern life more than any ruler of his age. The word \"algebra\" comes from the title of his most famous book, and the word \"algorithm\" is derived from his name. Every time we use a search engine, we are relying on ideas that he helped to develop. Ibn Sina's \"Canon of Medicine\" was studied in European universities for centuries. In recent decades, historians have been reassessing its influence, and many now argue that it shaped medical education far beyond the Islamic world. Legacies are not only for famous people, however. A grandmother who has been telling the same stories to three generations, a teacher whose former students are now teaching others, a volunteer who has planted trees that will shade people she will never meet: each of them is building something that will last. The question, then, is not whether we will leave a legacy, but what kind. We are writing ours every day.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Has Shaped, Has Been Teaching, Is Being Modest: Aspect for Stance and Relevance”. Let’s learn choosing aspect to show stance: present perfect for present relevance or ongoing influence (has outlived, has shaped) vs past simple for a finished past (founded, wrote); present perfect continuous for ongoing or recent activity and duration (has been teaching, have been reassessing); past perfect for background events in narratives (had inherited); present continuous for temporary situations, trends and annoying habits (is becoming, is always complaining); be being + adjective for temporary behavior (He's being modest); stative verbs with dynamic meanings (I'm thinking of…, She's having lunch); present simple for the current stance of sources (Historians argue…) together. Listen to the start of “Lives That Outlast Us”: What does it mean to leave a legacy? For some, it is a building or a fortune; for others, it is an idea that has outlived its creator by centuries. Look at the green words. Past simple presents an event as finished and separate from now: Al-Fihri founded the university in 859. Present perfect connects the past to the present – the result or influence still matters: The idea has outlived its creator. Al-Khwarizmi has influenced modern life. A writer can use this choice to show stance: \"Ibn Sina was a great doctor\" (history) vs \"Ibn Sina has shaped medicine\" (still relevant). Present perfect continuous stresses duration or an ongoing / recent activity: The university has been teaching students for eleven centuries. Historians have been reassessing his work. Past perfect sets up background in a narrative: She had inherited a fortune before she founded the university. Use the present simple to report the current views of sources: Many historians argue that… Here are some examples. The idea has outlived its creator by centuries. Fatima al-Fihri founded al-Qarawiyyin in 859. The university has been teaching students for eleven centuries. Be careful! Some learners say: “Fatima al-Fihri has founded al-Qarawiyyin in 859.” That’s not right. We say: “Fatima al-Fihri founded al-Qarawiyyin in 859.” Finished time (859) → past simple. Quick check: \"Fatima al-Fihri founded al-Qarawiyyin in 859.\" Why past simple? … Think! … A finished time in the past (859). Great job! Now you can say: I can explain the difference between \"Al-Fihri founded the university\" and \"The university has been teaching students for eleven centuries.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.05"}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS2","title":"Grammar for Style: Combining, Varying and Emphasizing","objectives":["Students will be able to combine short sentences into one sophisticated sentence using a range of advanced structures.","Students will be able to choose structures that create emphasis and variety in their writing.","I can turn three short sentences into one well-built sentence.","I can use a cleft sentence or inversion to emphasize the most important idea."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من دمج جمل قصيرة في جملة واحدة رفيعة باستخدام مجموعة من التراكيب المتقدمة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من اختيار التراكيب التي تحقق التوكيد والتنوّع في كتابتهم.","أستطيع أن أحوّل ثلاث جمل قصيرة إلى جملة واحدة محكمة البناء.","أستطيع أن أستخدم الجملة المشطورة أو القلب لتوكيد أهم فكرة."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"posthumous","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈpɑstʃʊməs/","definition":"happening after a person's death","arabic":"بعد الوفاة","example":"The novel was a posthumous success.","image_id":"GV-L12-U6-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS2-W01"},{"word":"commemorate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kəˈmɛmɚˌeɪt/","definition":"to remember and honor an important person or event","arabic":"يُحيي ذكرى","example":"A statue commemorates the city's founder.","image_id":"GV-L12-U6-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS2-W02"},{"word":"perpetuate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/pɚˈpɛtʃəˌweɪt/","definition":"to make something continue for a long time","arabic":"يُديم / يُخلّد","example":"The festival perpetuates an ancient tradition.","image_id":"GV-L12-U6-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS2-W03"},{"word":"bequeath","pos":"verb","ipa":"/bɪˈkwiθ/","definition":"to leave property or ideas to others after you die","arabic":"يورّث / يوصي بـ","example":"He bequeathed his library to the university.","image_id":"GV-L12-U6-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Advanced grammar is a toolbox for style. Use it to combine short, choppy sentences: Fatima al-Fihri was a merchant's daughter. She inherited a fortune. She founded a university. → A merchant's daughter, Fatima al-Fihri used her inherited fortune to found a university. (appositive + nominalization) → Having inherited a fortune, Fatima al-Fihri founded a university. (participle phrase)\nUse structures for emphasis: cleft sentences (It was al-Khwarizmi who gave us the word \"algebra.\" What made the university special was its openness to all.); fronting and inversion (Never had the city seen such a library. So great was her generosity that…). Put new or important information at the end of the sentence (end focus): The word \"algorithm\" comes from the name of a ninth-century mathematician.\nVary your sentences: mix short and long; begin some sentences with a participle phrase, a prepositional phrase or a subordinate clause instead of always starting with the subject. But choose clarity first: the best version is often the most concise one, not the most complicated. Ask: Is the most important idea in the main clause? Is anything repeated unnecessarily?\ncombine: relative clause • participle phrase • absolute • appositive • nominalization\nemphasize: It was… who / that… • What… was… • Never had… • So… that\nend focus: important or new information at the end\nvary openings and length – but clarity and concision first","examples":["Having inherited a fortune, Fatima al-Fihri founded a university.","A merchant's daughter, Fatima al-Fihri invested her fortune in learning.","It was al-Khwarizmi who gave us the word \"algebra.\"","What made the library special was its openness to all.","Never had the city seen such a collection of books.","So great was her generosity that students came from across North Africa.","The word \"algorithm\" comes from the name of a ninth-century mathematician.","Its walls covered in ancient tiles, the courtyard is still used for study."],"common_errors":["✗ Having inherited a fortune, a university was founded by Fatima al-Fihri. → ✓ Having inherited a fortune, Fatima al-Fihri founded a university. (Avoid a dangling participle.)","✗ It was al-Khwarizmi which gave us the word \"algebra.\" → ✓ It was al-Khwarizmi who gave us the word \"algebra.\" (Person → who.)","✗ So great her generosity was that students came from far away. → ✓ So great was her generosity that students came from far away. (Inversion.)","✗ The library, which it was built in 1975, which has many manuscripts, is famous. → ✓ The library, which was built in 1975 and has many manuscripts, is famous. (Combine clauses concisely.)"],"arabic":"القواعد المتقدمة صندوق أدوات للأسلوب: ندمج الجمل القصيرة المتقطعة بجمل الوصل وعبارات اسم الفاعل والتراكيب المطلقة والبدل والتسمية.\nللتوكيد نستخدم الجملة المشطورة (It was… who / What… was) والتقديم والقلب (Never had… / So great was… that).\nنضع المعلومة الجديدة أو المهمة في آخر الجملة (التركيز الختامي)، وننوّع بدايات الجمل وأطوالها.\nالوضوح أولًا: أفضل نسخة غالبًا هي الأوجز لا الأعقد."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Grammar for Style: Combining, Varying and Emphasizing”. Let’s learn mastery review of grammar for style: combining short sentences with relative clauses, participle phrases, absolute constructions, appositives and nominalization; emphasizing with cleft sentences (It was… who…; What… was…), fronting and inversion (Never had…, So great was…); varying sentence openings and length; end focus (putting new or important information last); choosing the most concise and effective version together.","on_screen":"GV-L12-U6-LS2 | Grammar for Style: Combining, Varying and Emphasizing","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: It was her grandmother who taught her to love books. What the scholar did not expect was such a large audience. (These are stylistic choices in statements.)","on_screen":"It was her grandmother who taught her to love books. | What the scholar did not expect was such a large audience. | (These are stylistic choices in statements.)","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Advanced grammar is a toolbox for style. Use it to combine short, choppy sentences: Fatima al-Fihri was a merchant's daughter. She inherited a fortune. She founded a university. → A merchant's daughter, Fatima al-Fihri used her inherited fortune to found a university. (appositive + nominalization) → Having inherited a fortune, Fatima al-Fihri founded a university. (participle phrase) Use structures for emphasis: cleft sentences (It was al-Khwarizmi who gave us the word \"algebra.\" What made the university special was its openness to all.); fronting and inversion (Never had the city seen such a library. So great was her generosity that…). Put new or important information at the end of the sentence (end focus): The word \"algorithm\" comes from the name of a ninth-century mathematician.","on_screen":"combine: relative clause • participle phrase • absolute • appositive • nominalization • emphasize: It was… who / that… • What… was… • Never had… • So… that • end focus: important or new information at the end","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Having inherited a fortune, Fatima al-Fihri founded a university. A merchant's daughter, Fatima al-Fihri invested her fortune in learning. It was al-Khwarizmi who gave us the word \"algebra.\"","on_screen":"Having inherited a fortune, Fatima al-Fihri founded a university. / A merchant's daughter, Fatima al-Fihri invested her fortune in learning. / It was al-Khwarizmi who gave us the word \"algebra.\"","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Having inherited a fortune, a university was founded by Fatima al-Fihri.” That’s not right. We say: “Having inherited a fortune, Fatima al-Fihri founded a university.” Avoid a dangling participle.","on_screen":"✗ Having inherited a fortune, a university was founded by Fatima al-Fihri.   ✓ Having inherited a fortune, Fatima al-Fihri founded a university.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:15","narration":"Quick check: How can we emphasize the person in \"Al-Khwarizmi gave us the word 'algebra'\"? … Think! … *It was al-Khwarizmi who gave us the word \"algebra.\"* Great job! Now you can say: I can turn three short sentences into one well-built sentence.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can turn three short sentences into one well-built sentence.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: mastery review of grammar for style: combining short sentences with relative clauses, participle phrases, absolute constructions, appositives and nominalization; emphasizing with cleft sentences (It was… who…; What… was…), fronting and inversion (Never had…, So great was…); varying sentence openings and length; end focus (putting new or important information last); choosing the most concise and effective version.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","القواعد المتقدمة صندوق أدوات للأسلوب: ندمج الجمل القصيرة المتقطعة بجمل الوصل وعبارات اسم الفاعل والتراكيب المطلقة والبدل والتسمية.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Having inherited a fortune, a university was founded by Fatima al-Fihri. — الصحيح: Having inherited a fortune, Fatima al-Fihri founded a university.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أحوّل ثلاث جمل قصيرة إلى جملة واحدة محكمة البناء."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the best answer.","items":[{"q":"Fatima al-Fihri inherited a fortune. She founded a university with it. → ___ a fortune, Fatima al-Fihri founded a university.","options":["Inheriting by","Having inherited","Inherited","Having been inherited"],"answer":"Having inherited","explanation":"Combining sentences with advanced structures.","explanation_ar":"دمج الجمل."},{"q":"___ al-Khwarizmi who gave us the word \"algebra.\"","options":["He was","That was","It was","There was"],"answer":"It was","explanation":"Cleft sentences for emphasis.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المشطورة."},{"q":"So great ___ that students came from across North Africa.","options":["her generosity","her generosity was","was her generosity","did her generosity"],"answer":"was her generosity","explanation":"Fronting and inversion for emphasis.","explanation_ar":"التقديم والقلب."},{"q":"___ made the library special was its openness to all.","options":["Which","It","That","What"],"answer":"What","explanation":"Cleft sentences for emphasis.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المشطورة."},{"q":"Which sentence has the clearest end focus on the most important information?","options":["The word \"algorithm\" comes from the name of a ninth-century mathematician.","The name, which a mathematician had, gave \"algorithm\" the word.","A ninth-century mathematician's name, the word \"algorithm\" comes from it.","From the name of a ninth-century mathematician, the word comes, \"algorithm\"."],"answer":"The word \"algorithm\" comes from the name of a ninth-century mathematician.","explanation":"End focus and concision.","explanation_ar":"التركيز الختامي والإيجاز."},{"q":"Ibn Sina wrote the \"Canon of Medicine.\" It was used in European universities for centuries. It is still studied by historians.\n\nWhich choice most effectively combines the three sentences?","options":["Ibn Sina, he wrote the \"Canon of Medicine,\" which it was used for centuries.","Ibn Sina's \"Canon of Medicine,\" which was used in European universities for centuries, is still studied by historians.","The \"Canon of Medicine\" was written, used and still studied, by Ibn Sina and universities and historians.","Ibn Sina wrote the \"Canon of Medicine,\" and it was used, and it is still studied."],"answer":"Ibn Sina's \"Canon of Medicine,\" which was used in European universities for centuries, is still studied by historians.","explanation":"Combining sentences with advanced structures.","explanation_ar":"دمج الجمل."}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS2-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Combine into one sentence.","items":[{"q":"Al-Qarawiyyin was founded in 859.  +  It is in Fez.  +  It is still teaching students. (appositive / relative clause)","options":[],"answer":"Al-Qarawiyyin, which was founded in Fez in 859, is still teaching students.","explanation":"Combining sentences with advanced structures.","explanation_ar":"دمج الجمل."},{"q":"My grandmother taught me to read.  +  I want to emphasize her. (It was… who)","options":[],"answer":"It was my grandmother who taught me to read.","explanation":"Cleft sentences for emphasis.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المشطورة."},{"q":"The city had never seen such a large library.  +  It opened in 1975. (Never had…)","options":[],"answer":"Never had the city seen such a large library as the one that opened in 1975.","explanation":"Fronting and inversion for emphasis.","explanation_ar":"التقديم والقلب."}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"Having inherited a fortune, a university was founded by her.","options":[],"answer":"Having inherited a fortune, she founded a university.","explanation":"Having inherited a fortune, a university was founded by her → Having inherited a fortune, she founded a university. Combining sentences with advanced structures.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Having inherited a fortune, a university was founded by her → Having inherited a fortune, she founded a university. دمج الجمل."},{"q":"It was the volunteers which restored the old manuscripts.","options":[],"answer":"It was the volunteers who restored the old manuscripts.","explanation":"which → who. Cleft sentences for emphasis.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: which → who. الجملة المشطورة."},{"q":"The library, which it was built in 1975, which has many manuscripts, is famous.","options":[],"answer":"The library, which was built in 1975 and has many manuscripts, is famous.","explanation":"which it was built in 1975, which has → which was built in 1975 and has. End focus and concision.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: which it was built in 1975, which has → which was built in 1975 and has. التركيز الختامي والإيجاز."}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Improve the style.","items":[{"q":"Combine: \"My grandfather was a teacher. He taught for forty years. He loved poetry.\"","options":[],"answer":"A lover of poetry, my grandfather taught for forty years.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mastery review of grammar for style: combining short sentences with relative clauses, participle phrases, absolute constructions, appositives and nominalization; emphasizing with cleft sentences (It was… who…; What… was…), fronting and inversion (Never had…, So great was…); varying sentence openings and length; end focus (putting new or important information last); choosing the most concise and effective version correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Emphasize the person: \"My mother encouraged me to study science.\"","options":[],"answer":"It was my mother who encouraged me to study science.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mastery review of grammar for style: combining short sentences with relative clauses, participle phrases, absolute constructions, appositives and nominalization; emphasizing with cleft sentences (It was… who…; What… was…), fronting and inversion (Never had…, So great was…); varying sentence openings and length; end focus (putting new or important information last); choosing the most concise and effective version correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Emphasize with \"What…\": \"Her kindness impressed me most.\"","options":[],"answer":"What impressed me most was her kindness.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mastery review of grammar for style: combining short sentences with relative clauses, participle phrases, absolute constructions, appositives and nominalization; emphasizing with cleft sentences (It was… who…; What… was…), fronting and inversion (Never had…, So great was…); varying sentence openings and length; end focus (putting new or important information last); choosing the most concise and effective version correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Rewrite with inversion: \"I had never seen such a beautiful manuscript.\"","options":[],"answer":"Never had I seen such a beautiful manuscript.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mastery review of grammar for style: combining short sentences with relative clauses, participle phrases, absolute constructions, appositives and nominalization; emphasizing with cleft sentences (It was… who…; What… was…), fronting and inversion (Never had…, So great was…); varying sentence openings and length; end focus (putting new or important information last); choosing the most concise and effective version correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Vary the opening: \"The museum opened in 2020. It has attracted many visitors.\"","options":[],"answer":"Since opening in 2020, the museum has attracted many visitors.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mastery review of grammar for style: combining short sentences with relative clauses, participle phrases, absolute constructions, appositives and nominalization; emphasizing with cleft sentences (It was… who…; What… was…), fronting and inversion (Never had…, So great was…); varying sentence openings and length; end focus (putting new or important information last); choosing the most concise and effective version correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Revise a paragraph.","items":[{"q":"Rewrite these choppy sentences as one or two sophisticated sentences: \"The scholar lived in Baghdad. He studied the stars. He wrote many books. His books were translated into Latin.\"","options":[],"answer":"A scholar who studied the stars in Baghdad, he wrote many books that were later translated into Latin.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mastery review of grammar for style: combining short sentences with relative clauses, participle phrases, absolute constructions, appositives and nominalization; emphasizing with cleft sentences (It was… who…; What… was…), fronting and inversion (Never had…, So great was…); varying sentence openings and length; end focus (putting new or important information last); choosing the most concise and effective version correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one cleft sentence and one inverted sentence about someone who influenced you.","options":[],"answer":"It was my uncle who first took me to a library. Never had I seen so many books in one place.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mastery review of grammar for style: combining short sentences with relative clauses, participle phrases, absolute constructions, appositives and nominalization; emphasizing with cleft sentences (It was… who…; What… was…), fronting and inversion (Never had…, So great was…); varying sentence openings and length; end focus (putting new or important information last); choosing the most concise and effective version correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Explain which version you prefer and why: \"She founded a school. It was in her village.\" or \"She founded a school in her village.\"","options":[],"answer":"I prefer the second version because it is shorter and clearer.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mastery review of grammar for style: combining short sentences with relative clauses, participle phrases, absolute constructions, appositives and nominalization; emphasizing with cleft sentences (It was… who…; What… was…), fronting and inversion (Never had…, So great was…); varying sentence openings and length; end focus (putting new or important information last); choosing the most concise and effective version correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Dice Sentences","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Turn over a cue card and roll the die.","Make a sentence with the cue in the form shown by the die.","The player on the left checks; a correct sentence wins the card.","The player with the most cards after 7 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"the idea / outlive / its creator (present perfect)"},{"cue":"the university / teach / for eleven centuries (present perfect continuous)"},{"cue":"she / inherit / a fortune / before she founded it (past perfect)"},{"cue":"we / rely / on his ideas / right now (present continuous)"},{"cue":"historians / reassess / his influence / recently (present perfect continuous)"},{"cue":"historians / argue / today (present for stance)"},{"cue":"he / be / modest / today (be being)"},{"cue":"I / think / about my future (dynamic)"},{"cue":"we / write / our legacy / every day"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The house was built in 1920. It belonged to my great-grandfather. → The house, ___, belonged to my great-grandfather.","options":["built in 1920","it was built in 1920","building in 1920","which built in 1920"],"answer":"built in 1920","explanation":"Combining sentences with advanced structures.","explanation_ar":"دمج الجمل."},{"q":"___ my teacher who first noticed my talent for writing.","options":["She was","It was","That was","There was"],"answer":"It was","explanation":"Cleft sentences for emphasis.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المشطورة."},{"q":"What I value most about my grandmother ___ her patience.","options":["does","are","was being","is"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Cleft sentences for emphasis.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المشطورة."},{"q":"Not until I read his letters ___ how much he had sacrificed.","options":["did I understand","understood I","I understood","I did understand"],"answer":"did I understand","explanation":"Fronting and inversion for emphasis.","explanation_ar":"التقديم والقلب."},{"q":"___ by generations of readers, the poem is still taught in schools.","options":["Having loved","Love","Loved","Loving"],"answer":"Loved","explanation":"Varying sentence openings.","explanation_ar":"تنويع بدايات الجمل."},{"q":"","options":["With shaking, the old calligrapher completed his final manuscript.","Her hands shaking, the old calligrapher completed his final manuscript.","Shaking, the old calligrapher's final manuscript was completed.","Her hands shaking, the final manuscript was completed by the old calligrapher."],"answer":"Her hands shaking, the old calligrapher completed his final manuscript.","explanation":"Combining sentences with advanced structures.","explanation_ar":"دمج الجمل."},{"q":"","options":["So beautiful the mosque was that visitors traveled for weeks to see it.","So beautiful was the mosque that visitors traveled for weeks to see it.","Such beautiful was the mosque that visitors traveled for weeks to see it.","So beautiful did the mosque that visitors traveled for weeks to see it."],"answer":"So beautiful was the mosque that visitors traveled for weeks to see it.","explanation":"Fronting and inversion for emphasis.","explanation_ar":"التقديم والقلب."},{"q":"The scholar donated his entire library to the city. The library contained ten thousand books. Many of them were rare.\n\nWhich choice most effectively combines the three sentences?","options":["The scholar donated to the city his library which it contained ten thousand books many rare.","The scholar's library, ten thousand books, was donated, many of them rare, to the city by him.","The scholar donated his library, and it contained ten thousand books, and many were rare, to the city.","The scholar donated his entire library of ten thousand books, many of them rare, to the city."],"answer":"The scholar donated his entire library of ten thousand books, many of them rare, to the city.","explanation":"Combining sentences with advanced structures.","explanation_ar":"دمج الجمل."},{"q":"Which sentence puts the new and most important information at the end?","options":["The university's founder was a woman named Fatima al-Fihri.","A woman named Fatima al-Fihri, the founder was of the university.","Fatima al-Fihri, a woman, was the university's founder named.","Was the university's founder Fatima al-Fihri, a woman?"],"answer":"The university's founder was a woman named Fatima al-Fihri.","explanation":"End focus and concision.","explanation_ar":"التركيز الختامي والإيجاز."},{"q":"What is usually the most important quality of a well-written sentence?","options":["complexity","length","clarity","the number of clauses"],"answer":"clarity","explanation":"End focus and concision.","explanation_ar":"التركيز الختامي والإيجاز."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A writer's desk: a draft full of short, choppy sentences on the left and a polished version on the right with colored highlights: \"relative clause\", \"participle phrase\", \"appositive\", \"cleft\", \"inversion\"; a sign \"Grammar is a toolbox for style\". Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A writer's desk: a draft full of short, choppy sentences on the left and a polished version on the right with colored highlights: \"relative clause\", \"participle phrase\", \"appositive\", \"cleft\", \"inversion\"; a sign \"Grammar is a toolbox for style\""},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of mastery review of grammar for style: combining short sentences with relative clauses, participle phrases, absolute constructions, appositives and nominalization; emphasizing with cleft sentences (It was… who…; What… was…), fronting and inversion (Never had…, So great was…); varying sentence openings and length; end focus (putting new or important information last); choosing the most concise and effective version: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Legacy”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of mastery review of grammar for style: combining short sentences with relative clauses, participle phrases, absolute constructions, appositives and nominalization"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows posthumous (happening after a person's death); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing posthumous: happening after a person's death"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows commemorate (to remember and honor an important person or event); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing commemorate: to remember and honor an important person or event"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows perpetuate (to make something continue for a long time); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing perpetuate: to make something continue for a long time"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows bequeath (to leave property or ideas to others after you die); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing bequeath: to leave property or ideas to others after you die"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Dice Sentences”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Dice Sentences"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS2-W01","script":"posthumous. posthumous. The novel was a posthumous success.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS2-W02","script":"commemorate. commemorate. A statue commemorates the city's founder.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS2-W03","script":"perpetuate. perpetuate. The festival perpetuates an ancient tradition.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS2-W04","script":"bequeath. bequeath. He bequeathed his library to the university.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Grammar for Style: Combining, Varying and Emphasizing”. Let’s learn mastery review of grammar for style: combining short sentences with relative clauses, participle phrases, absolute constructions, appositives and nominalization; emphasizing with cleft sentences (It was… who…; What… was…), fronting and inversion (Never had…, So great was…); varying sentence openings and length; end focus (putting new or important information last); choosing the most concise and effective version together. Remember these patterns: It was her grandmother who taught her to love books. What the scholar did not expect was such a large audience. (These are stylistic choices in statements.) Advanced grammar is a toolbox for style. Use it to combine short, choppy sentences: Fatima al-Fihri was a merchant's daughter. She inherited a fortune. She founded a university. → A merchant's daughter, Fatima al-Fihri used her inherited fortune to found a university. (appositive + nominalization) → Having inherited a fortune, Fatima al-Fihri founded a university. (participle phrase) Use structures for emphasis: cleft sentences (It was al-Khwarizmi who gave us the word \"algebra.\" What made the university special was its openness to all.); fronting and inversion (Never had the city seen such a library. So great was her generosity that…). Put new or important information at the end of the sentence (end focus): The word \"algorithm\" comes from the name of a ninth-century mathematician. Here are some examples. Having inherited a fortune, Fatima al-Fihri founded a university. A merchant's daughter, Fatima al-Fihri invested her fortune in learning. It was al-Khwarizmi who gave us the word \"algebra.\" Be careful! Some learners say: “Having inherited a fortune, a university was founded by Fatima al-Fihri.” That’s not right. We say: “Having inherited a fortune, Fatima al-Fihri founded a university.” Avoid a dangling participle. Quick check: How can we emphasize the person in \"Al-Khwarizmi gave us the word 'algebra'\"? … Think! … *It was al-Khwarizmi who gave us the word \"algebra.\"* Great job! Now you can say: I can turn three short sentences into one well-built sentence.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.05"}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3","title":"Pave the Way, Stand the Test of Time: Legacy Idioms and Collocations","objectives":["Students will be able to describe the achievements and influence of people with legacy idioms and collocations.","Students will be able to choose precise legacy vocabulary in formal and informal contexts.","I can say \"She paved the way for women in science\" and \"His work has stood the test of time.\"","I can describe \"a seminal work\" and \"a family heirloom\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من وصف إنجازات الناس وأثرهم بتعابير الإرث ومتلازماته.","سيتمكن الطلاب من اختيار مفردات الإرث الدقيقة في السياقات الرسمية وغير الرسمية.","أستطيع أن أقول She paved the way for women in science وHis work has stood the test of time.","أستطيع أن أصف a seminal work وa family heirloom."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"testament","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtɛstəmənt/","definition":"something that clearly shows that something is true or exists","arabic":"شاهد / دليل","example":"The mosque is a testament to the skill of its builders.","image_id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS3-W01"},{"word":"immortalize","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˌɪˈmɔrtəlaɪz/","definition":"to make someone or something remembered forever","arabic":"يخلّد","example":"The poet immortalized his hometown in verse.","image_id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS3-W02"},{"word":"seminal","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈsɛmənəl/","definition":"very important and influencing later developments","arabic":"رائد / مؤسِّس","example":"It was a seminal work in the history of mathematics.","image_id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS3-W03"},{"word":"monumental","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌmɑnjəˈmɛntəl/","definition":"very large, important or impressive","arabic":"ضخم / عظيم الأثر","example":"Building the canal was a monumental achievement.","image_id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS3-W04"},{"word":"revere","pos":"verb","ipa":"/rɪˈvɪr/","definition":"to respect and admire someone deeply","arabic":"يُجلّ / يوقّر","example":"The scholar is revered across the Arab world.","image_id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS3-W05"},{"word":"endowment","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɛnˈdaʊmənt/","definition":"money given to an institution to provide a regular income","arabic":"وقف / منحة دائمة","example":"The university's endowment funds hundreds of scholarships.","image_id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-W06","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS3-W06"},{"word":"heirloom","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɛrˌlum/","definition":"a valuable object passed down through a family","arabic":"إرث عائلي / تحفة متوارثة","example":"This silver coffee pot is a family heirloom.","image_id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-W07","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS3-W07"}],"explanation":{"text":"Legacy words: a pioneer / trailblazer (the first to do something), an enduring influence (lasting), posterity (future generations), posthumous (after death: a posthumous award), commemorate (honor the memory of), perpetuate (make something continue), bequeath (leave to others after death), a testament to (clear proof of), immortalize (make remembered forever), seminal (very influential and original), monumental (huge and important), revere (deeply respect), an endowment (money that provides regular income), an heirloom (a family treasure).\nIdioms: leave a legacy; pave the way for (make something possible for others); stand the test of time (remain good or relevant for a long time); leave one's mark on; be ahead of one's time (have ideas too modern for one's era); pass the torch to (hand over responsibility); follow in someone's footsteps (do what a parent or mentor did); stand on the shoulders of giants (build on the work of great people before you); blaze a trail (be a trailblazer); a household name (someone everyone knows).\nCollocations: an enduring legacy; a lasting impact; a seminal work / study; a monumental achievement; a fitting tribute; a family heirloom; preserve something for posterity; in memory of; a testament to her skill. Register: idioms suit speeches and informal writing; in formal reports, prefer precise words (pioneered, influenced, had a lasting impact on).\nCollocations/phrases: leave a legacy • pave the way for • stand the test of time • leave one's mark on | ahead of one's time • pass the torch to • follow in someone's footsteps • stand on the shoulders of giants | an enduring legacy • a seminal work • a monumental achievement • a fitting tribute | a family heirloom • for posterity • in memory of • a testament to","examples":["Fatima al-Fihri left a legacy that has lasted for more than eleven centuries.","She paved the way for women in education.","Al-Khwarizmi's ideas have stood the test of time.","The scientist was ahead of her time.","The old coach finally passed the torch to his former student.","She followed in her father's footsteps and became a doctor.","The mosque is a testament to the skill of its builders.","This silver coffee pot is a family heirloom."],"common_errors":["✗ She paved the road for women scientists. → ✓ She paved the way for women scientists. (Fixed idiom.)","✗ His work has stood the test of the time. → ✓ His work has stood the test of time. (No the.)","✗ The award was given to him posthumously while he was alive. → ✓ The award was given to him posthumously, after his death. (posthumous = after death.)","✗ The museum commemorates to the city's founder. → ✓ The museum commemorates the city's founder. (No to.)"],"arabic":"كلمات الإرث: pioneer / trailblazer (رائد) وenduring (دائم) وposterity (الأجيال القادمة) وposthumous (بعد الوفاة) وcommemorate (يحيي الذكرى) وbequeath (يورّث) وtestament (شاهد) وseminal (مؤسِّس) وheirloom (إرث عائلي).\nتعابير: leave a legacy (يترك إرثًا) وpave the way for (يمهّد الطريق) وstand the test of time (يصمد أمام الزمن) وahead of one's time (سابق لعصره) وfollow in someone's footsteps (يسير على خطاه) وstand on the shoulders of giants.\nالتعابير مناسبة للخطب والكتابة غير الرسمية، أما التقارير الرسمية فنفضّل فيها الكلمات الدقيقة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Pave the Way, Stand the Test of Time: Legacy Idioms and Collocations”. Let’s learn legacy vocabulary (pioneer, enduring, trailblazer, posterity, posthumous, commemorate, perpetuate, bequeath, testament, immortalize, seminal, monumental, revere, endowment, heirloom); idioms (leave a legacy, pave the way, stand the test of time, leave one's mark, ahead of one's time, pass the torch, follow in someone's footsteps, stand on the shoulders of giants, blaze a trail, a household name); collocations (an enduring legacy, a lasting impact, a seminal work, a monumental achievement, a fitting tribute, a family heirloom, for posterity, in memory of) together.","on_screen":"GV-L12-U6-LS3 | Pave the Way, Stand the Test of Time: Legacy Idioms and Collocations","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. testament: something that clearly shows that something is true or exists. immortalize: to make someone or something remembered forever. seminal: very important and influencing later developments.","on_screen":"testament | immortalize | seminal","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Legacy words: a pioneer / trailblazer (the first to do something), an enduring influence (lasting), posterity (future generations), posthumous (after death: a posthumous award), commemorate (honor the memory of), perpetuate (make something continue), bequeath (leave to others after death), a testament to (clear proof of), immortalize (make remembered forever), seminal (very influential and original), monumental (huge and important), revere (deeply respect), an endowment (money that provides regular income), an heirloom (a family treasure). Idioms: leave a legacy; pave the way for (make something possible for others); stand the test of time (remain good or relevant for a long time); leave one's mark on; be ahead of one's time (have ideas too modern for one's era); pass the torch to (hand over responsibility); follow in someone's footsteps (do what a parent or mentor did); stand on the shoulders of giants (build on the work of great people before you); blaze a trail (be a trailblazer); a household name (someone everyone knows).","on_screen":"legacy vocabulary (pioneer, enduring, trailblazer, posterity, posthumous, commemorate, perpetuate, bequeath, testament, immortalize, seminal, monumental, revere, endowment, heirloom); idioms (leave a legacy, pave the way, stand the test of time, leave one's mark, ahead of one's time, pass the torch, follow in someone's footsteps, stand on the shoulders of giants, blaze a trail, a household name); collocations (an enduring legacy, a lasting impact, a seminal work, a monumental achievement, a fitting tribute, a family heirloom, for posterity, in memory of)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Fatima al-Fihri left a legacy that has lasted for more than eleven centuries. She paved the way for women in education. Al-Khwarizmi's ideas have stood the test of time.","on_screen":"Fatima al-Fihri left a legacy that has lasted for more than eleven centuries. / She paved the way for women in education. / Al-Khwarizmi's ideas have stood the test of time.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “She paved the road for women scientists.” That’s not right. We say: “She paved the way for women scientists.” Fixed idiom.","on_screen":"✗ She paved the road for women scientists.   ✓ She paved the way for women scientists.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:15","narration":"Quick check: What does \"ahead of her time\" mean? … Think! … Her ideas were too modern for her era. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"She paved the way for women in science\" and \"His work has stood the test of time.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"She paved the way for women in science\" and \"His work has stood the test of time.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: legacy vocabulary (pioneer, enduring, trailblazer, posterity, posthumous, commemorate, perpetuate, bequeath, testament, immortalize, seminal, monumental, revere, endowment, heirloom); idioms (leave a legacy, pave the way, stand the test of time, leave one's mark, ahead of one's time, pass the torch, follow in someone's footsteps, stand on the shoulders of giants, blaze a trail, a household name); collocations (an enduring legacy, a lasting impact, a seminal work, a monumental achievement, a fitting tribute, a family heirloom, for posterity, in memory of).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","كلمات الإرث: pioneer / trailblazer (رائد) وenduring (دائم) وposterity (الأجيال القادمة) وposthumous (بعد الوفاة) وcommemorate (يحيي الذكرى) وbequeath (يورّث) وtestament (شاهد) وseminal (مؤسِّس) وheirloom (إرث عائلي).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: She paved the road for women scientists. — الصحيح: She paved the way for women scientists.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول She paved the way for women in science وHis work has stood the test of time."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Fatima al-Fihri ___ for women in education.","options":["paved the road","built the path","made the way","paved the way"],"answer":"paved the way","explanation":"Legacy idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"Al-Khwarizmi's ideas have stood the test of ___.","options":["the time","times","timing","time"],"answer":"time","explanation":"Legacy idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"The scientist's ideas were so modern that she was ahead of her ___.","options":["time","clock","days","era's"],"answer":"time","explanation":"Legacy idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"She followed in her father's ___ and became a surgeon.","options":["feet","steps on","footsteps","shoes"],"answer":"footsteps","explanation":"Legacy idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"This silver coffee pot, passed down through five generations, is a family ___.","options":["testament","endowment","heirloom","posterity"],"answer":"heirloom","explanation":"Legacy word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Published in the ninth century, al-Khwarizmi's book on algebra is considered a ______ work, since it shaped the development of mathematics for centuries afterward.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["reverent","seminal","monumental in size","posthumous"],"answer":"seminal","explanation":"Words in context (SAT style).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات في السياق."}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the word or idiom to its meaning.","items":[{"q":"posterity","options":["to leave property or ideas to others after death","to remember and honor an important person or event","to build on the work of great people before you","a person whom almost everyone knows","to hand over responsibility to the next generation","all the people who will live in the future"],"answer":"all the people who will live in the future","explanation":"posterity → all the people who will live in the future. Legacy idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"bequeath","options":["to leave property or ideas to others after death","to remember and honor an important person or event","to build on the work of great people before you","a person whom almost everyone knows","to hand over responsibility to the next generation","all the people who will live in the future"],"answer":"to leave property or ideas to others after death","explanation":"bequeath → to leave property or ideas to others after death. Legacy idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"commemorate","options":["to leave property or ideas to others after death","to remember and honor an important person or event","to build on the work of great people before you","a person whom almost everyone knows","to hand over responsibility to the next generation","all the people who will live in the future"],"answer":"to remember and honor an important person or event","explanation":"commemorate → to remember and honor an important person or event. Legacy idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"pass the torch","options":["to leave property or ideas to others after death","to remember and honor an important person or event","to build on the work of great people before you","a person whom almost everyone knows","to hand over responsibility to the next generation","all the people who will live in the future"],"answer":"to hand over responsibility to the next generation","explanation":"pass the torch → to hand over responsibility to the next generation. Legacy idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"stand on the shoulders of giants","options":["to leave property or ideas to others after death","to remember and honor an important person or event","to build on the work of great people before you","a person whom almost everyone knows","to hand over responsibility to the next generation","all the people who will live in the future"],"answer":"to build on the work of great people before you","explanation":"stand on the shoulders of giants → to build on the work of great people before you. Legacy idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"a household name","options":["to leave property or ideas to others after death","to remember and honor an important person or event","to build on the work of great people before you","a person whom almost everyone knows","to hand over responsibility to the next generation","all the people who will live in the future"],"answer":"a person whom almost everyone knows","explanation":"a household name → a person whom almost everyone knows. Legacy idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Talk about legacy.","items":[{"q":"Name someone who paved the way for others in your country or community.","options":[],"answer":"My grandmother paved the way for girls in our village to go to school.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses legacy vocabulary (pioneer, enduring, trailblazer, posterity, posthumous, commemorate, perpetuate, bequeath, testament, immortalize, seminal, monumental, revere, endowment, heirloom); idioms (leave a legacy, pave the way, stand the test of time, leave one's mark, ahead of one's time, pass the torch, follow in someone's footsteps, stand on the shoulders of giants, blaze a trail, a household name); collocations (an enduring legacy, a lasting impact, a seminal work, a monumental achievement, a fitting tribute, a family heirloom, for posterity, in memory of) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Name a book, building or idea that has stood the test of time.","options":[],"answer":"The Masjid al-Haram has stood the test of time as a center of faith and learning.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses legacy vocabulary (pioneer, enduring, trailblazer, posterity, posthumous, commemorate, perpetuate, bequeath, testament, immortalize, seminal, monumental, revere, endowment, heirloom); idioms (leave a legacy, pave the way, stand the test of time, leave one's mark, ahead of one's time, pass the torch, follow in someone's footsteps, stand on the shoulders of giants, blaze a trail, a household name); collocations (an enduring legacy, a lasting impact, a seminal work, a monumental achievement, a fitting tribute, a family heirloom, for posterity, in memory of) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Do you want to follow in someone's footsteps? Whose?","options":[],"answer":"I want to follow in my uncle's footsteps and become an engineer.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses legacy vocabulary (pioneer, enduring, trailblazer, posterity, posthumous, commemorate, perpetuate, bequeath, testament, immortalize, seminal, monumental, revere, endowment, heirloom); idioms (leave a legacy, pave the way, stand the test of time, leave one's mark, ahead of one's time, pass the torch, follow in someone's footsteps, stand on the shoulders of giants, blaze a trail, a household name); collocations (an enduring legacy, a lasting impact, a seminal work, a monumental achievement, a fitting tribute, a family heirloom, for posterity, in memory of) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Describe a family heirloom you know about.","options":[],"answer":"My family has an old dagger that belonged to my great-grandfather.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses legacy vocabulary (pioneer, enduring, trailblazer, posterity, posthumous, commemorate, perpetuate, bequeath, testament, immortalize, seminal, monumental, revere, endowment, heirloom); idioms (leave a legacy, pave the way, stand the test of time, leave one's mark, ahead of one's time, pass the torch, follow in someone's footsteps, stand on the shoulders of giants, blaze a trail, a household name); collocations (an enduring legacy, a lasting impact, a seminal work, a monumental achievement, a fitting tribute, a family heirloom, for posterity, in memory of) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"a testament to\".","options":[],"answer":"The restored old town is a testament to the skill of local craftsmen.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses legacy vocabulary (pioneer, enduring, trailblazer, posterity, posthumous, commemorate, perpetuate, bequeath, testament, immortalize, seminal, monumental, revere, endowment, heirloom); idioms (leave a legacy, pave the way, stand the test of time, leave one's mark, ahead of one's time, pass the torch, follow in someone's footsteps, stand on the shoulders of giants, blaze a trail, a household name); collocations (an enduring legacy, a lasting impact, a seminal work, a monumental achievement, a fitting tribute, a family heirloom, for posterity, in memory of) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: A tribute.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 sentences paying tribute to someone, using 3 idioms or collocations.","options":[],"answer":"My teacher left a lasting impact on everyone she taught. She paved the way for many of us to study abroad. Her kindness will stand the test of time.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses legacy vocabulary (pioneer, enduring, trailblazer, posterity, posthumous, commemorate, perpetuate, bequeath, testament, immortalize, seminal, monumental, revere, endowment, heirloom); idioms (leave a legacy, pave the way, stand the test of time, leave one's mark, ahead of one's time, pass the torch, follow in someone's footsteps, stand on the shoulders of giants, blaze a trail, a household name); collocations (an enduring legacy, a lasting impact, a seminal work, a monumental achievement, a fitting tribute, a family heirloom, for posterity, in memory of) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences: one informal (with an idiom) and one formal (without) about the same person.","options":[],"answer":"She was ahead of her time. Her ideas anticipated developments that occurred decades later.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses legacy vocabulary (pioneer, enduring, trailblazer, posterity, posthumous, commemorate, perpetuate, bequeath, testament, immortalize, seminal, monumental, revere, endowment, heirloom); idioms (leave a legacy, pave the way, stand the test of time, leave one's mark, ahead of one's time, pass the torch, follow in someone's footsteps, stand on the shoulders of giants, blaze a trail, a household name); collocations (an enduring legacy, a lasting impact, a seminal work, a monumental achievement, a fitting tribute, a family heirloom, for posterity, in memory of) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with \"for posterity\".","options":[],"answer":"The family recorded the grandmother's stories for posterity.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses legacy vocabulary (pioneer, enduring, trailblazer, posterity, posthumous, commemorate, perpetuate, bequeath, testament, immortalize, seminal, monumental, revere, endowment, heirloom); idioms (leave a legacy, pave the way, stand the test of time, leave one's mark, ahead of one's time, pass the torch, follow in someone's footsteps, stand on the shoulders of giants, blaze a trail, a household name); collocations (an enduring legacy, a lasting impact, a seminal work, a monumental achievement, a fitting tribute, a family heirloom, for posterity, in memory of) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Vocabulary Bingo","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Students write nine words from the list in their grid.","The teacher (or a student caller) reads a definition or Arabic meaning.","Students cross out the matching word.","Three in a row = \"Bingo!\" The winner must read the words and say what each means."],"data":[{"word":"pioneer","match":"one of the first people to do something new","arabic":"رائد"},{"word":"enduring","match":"lasting for a long time","arabic":"دائم / باقٍ"},{"word":"trailblazer","match":"a person who is the first to do something and shows others the way","arabic":"رائد يشقّ الطريق"},{"word":"posterity","match":"all the people who will live in the future","arabic":"الأجيال القادمة"},{"word":"posthumous","match":"happening after a person's death","arabic":"بعد الوفاة"},{"word":"commemorate","match":"to remember and honor an important person or event","arabic":"يُحيي ذكرى"},{"word":"perpetuate","match":"to make something continue for a long time","arabic":"يُديم / يُخلّد"},{"word":"bequeath","match":"to leave property or ideas to others after you die","arabic":"يورّث / يوصي بـ"},{"word":"testament","match":"something that clearly shows that something is true or exists","arabic":"شاهد / دليل"},{"word":"immortalize","match":"to make someone or something remembered forever","arabic":"يخلّد"},{"word":"seminal","match":"very important and influencing later developments","arabic":"رائد / مؤسِّس"},{"word":"monumental","match":"very large, important or impressive","arabic":"ضخم / عظيم الأثر"},{"word":"revere","match":"to respect and admire someone deeply","arabic":"يُجلّ / يوقّر"},{"word":"endowment","match":"money given to an institution to provide a regular income","arabic":"وقف / منحة دائمة"},{"word":"heirloom","match":"a valuable object passed down through a family","arabic":"إرث عائلي / تحفة متوارثة"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The old poet is ___ throughout the Arab world.","options":["revered","commemorated to","bequeathed","perpetuated"],"answer":"revered","explanation":"Legacy word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"A statue in the main square ___ the city's founder.","options":["reveres to","bequeaths","perpetuates of","commemorates"],"answer":"commemorates","explanation":"Legacy word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"In his will, he ___ his entire library to the university.","options":["revered","bequeathed","immortalized","commemorated"],"answer":"bequeathed","explanation":"Legacy word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"The novel became a ___ success; sadly, the author had died a year earlier.","options":["posthumous","enduring","monumental","seminal"],"answer":"posthumous","explanation":"Legacy word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"The university's ___ provides scholarships for hundreds of students every year.","options":["testament","heirloom","endowment","posterity"],"answer":"endowment","explanation":"Legacy word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"She was a ___ for women in engineering in the 1980s.","options":["heirloom","trailblazer","posterity","household name"],"answer":"trailblazer","explanation":"Legacy idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"Building the new railway across the desert was a ___ achievement.","options":["monumental","posthumous","reverent","seminal in time"],"answer":"monumental","explanation":"Legacy collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة."},{"q":"The festival ___ an ancient tradition of poetry competitions.","options":["revers","posthumes","perpetuates","bequeaths"],"answer":"perpetuates","explanation":"Legacy word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"The poet ______ his hometown in a series of poems that are still recited in schools across the region.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["bequeathed","commemorated to","immortalized","endowed"],"answer":"immortalized","explanation":"Words in context (SAT style).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات في السياق."},{"q":"The restored eighteenth-century houses of the old district are a ______ to the skill of the craftsmen who built them without modern tools.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["endowment","posterity","heirloom","testament"],"answer":"testament","explanation":"Words in context (SAT style).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات في السياق."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A \"Hall of Legacy\" exhibition: portraits of historical scholars, a display case with a family heirloom (an old silver coffee pot), a plaque reading \"In memory of…\", and a timeline titled \"They Paved the Way\". Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A \"Hall of Legacy\" exhibition: portraits of historical scholars, a display case with a family heirloom (an old silver coffee pot), a plaque reading \"In memory of…\", and a timeline titled \"They Paved the Way\""},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 7 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 7 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows testament (something that clearly shows that something is true or exists); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing testament: something that clearly shows that something is true or exists"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows immortalize (to make someone or something remembered forever); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing immortalize: to make someone or something remembered forever"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows seminal (very important and influencing later developments); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing seminal: very important and influencing later developments"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows monumental (very large, important or impressive); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing monumental: very large, important or impressive"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows revere (to respect and admire someone deeply); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing revere: to respect and admire someone deeply"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-W06","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows endowment (money given to an institution to provide a regular income); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing endowment: money given to an institution to provide a regular income"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-W07","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows heirloom (a valuable object passed down through a family); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing heirloom: a valuable object passed down through a family"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Vocabulary Bingo”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Vocabulary Bingo"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS3-W01","script":"testament. testament. The mosque is a testament to the skill of its builders.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS3-W02","script":"immortalize. immortalize. The poet immortalized his hometown in verse.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS3-W03","script":"seminal. seminal. It was a seminal work in the history of mathematics.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS3-W04","script":"monumental. monumental. Building the canal was a monumental achievement.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS3-W05","script":"revere. revere. The scholar is revered across the Arab world.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS3-W06","script":"endowment. endowment. The university's endowment funds hundreds of scholarships.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS3-W07","script":"heirloom. heirloom. This silver coffee pot is a family heirloom.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Pave the Way, Stand the Test of Time: Legacy Idioms and Collocations”. Let’s learn legacy vocabulary (pioneer, enduring, trailblazer, posterity, posthumous, commemorate, perpetuate, bequeath, testament, immortalize, seminal, monumental, revere, endowment, heirloom); idioms (leave a legacy, pave the way, stand the test of time, leave one's mark, ahead of one's time, pass the torch, follow in someone's footsteps, stand on the shoulders of giants, blaze a trail, a household name); collocations (an enduring legacy, a lasting impact, a seminal work, a monumental achievement, a fitting tribute, a family heirloom, for posterity, in memory of) together. Meet some new words. testament: something that clearly shows that something is true or exists. immortalize: to make someone or something remembered forever. seminal: very important and influencing later developments. Legacy words: a pioneer / trailblazer (the first to do something), an enduring influence (lasting), posterity (future generations), posthumous (after death: a posthumous award), commemorate (honor the memory of), perpetuate (make something continue), bequeath (leave to others after death), a testament to (clear proof of), immortalize (make remembered forever), seminal (very influential and original), monumental (huge and important), revere (deeply respect), an endowment (money that provides regular income), an heirloom (a family treasure). Idioms: leave a legacy; pave the way for (make something possible for others); stand the test of time (remain good or relevant for a long time); leave one's mark on; be ahead of one's time (have ideas too modern for one's era); pass the torch to (hand over responsibility); follow in someone's footsteps (do what a parent or mentor did); stand on the shoulders of giants (build on the work of great people before you); blaze a trail (be a trailblazer); a household name (someone everyone knows). Here are some examples. Fatima al-Fihri left a legacy that has lasted for more than eleven centuries. She paved the way for women in education. Al-Khwarizmi's ideas have stood the test of time. Be careful! Some learners say: “She paved the road for women scientists.” That’s not right. We say: “She paved the way for women scientists.” Fixed idiom. Quick check: What does \"ahead of her time\" mean? … Think! … Her ideas were too modern for her era. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"She paved the way for women in science\" and \"His work has stood the test of time.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.05"}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS4","title":"The Final Edit: Comprehensive Conventions Review (SAT)","objectives":["Students will be able to identify and correct errors in all the major conventions of Standard English.","Students will be able to answer mixed SAT conventions questions by first identifying the skill being tested.","I can identify which convention an SAT question is testing before I answer it.","I can edit a paragraph that contains several different types of errors."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تحديد الأخطاء وتصحيحها في جميع قواعد الإنجليزية المعيارية الرئيسة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من الإجابة عن أسئلة القواعد المختلطة بنمط SAT بتحديد المهارة المختبرة أولًا.","أستطيع أن أحدد القاعدة التي يختبرها سؤال SAT قبل أن أجيب.","أستطيع أن أحرّر فقرة تحتوي على أنواع مختلفة من الأخطاء."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"pioneer","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌpaɪəˈnɪr/","definition":"one of the first people to do something new","arabic":"رائد","example":"Ibn Sina was a pioneer of modern medicine.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"enduring","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ɛndˈjʊrɪŋ/","definition":"lasting for a long time","arabic":"دائم / باقٍ","example":"Her poems have had an enduring influence.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"trailblazer","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtreɪlˌbleɪzɚ/","definition":"a person who is the first to do something and shows others the way","arabic":"رائد يشقّ الطريق","example":"She was a trailblazer for women in science.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"posterity","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pɑˈstɛrəti/","definition":"all the people who will live in the future","arabic":"الأجيال القادمة","example":"The letters were preserved for posterity.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"posthumous","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈpɑstʃʊməs/","definition":"happening after a person's death","arabic":"بعد الوفاة","example":"The novel was a posthumous success.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"commemorate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kəˈmɛmɚˌeɪt/","definition":"to remember and honor an important person or event","arabic":"يُحيي ذكرى","example":"A statue commemorates the city's founder.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"SAT conventions questions test a small set of skills again and again. Step 1: look at how the options differ. If they differ in punctuation, it is a boundary or punctuation question. If they differ in verb forms, check agreement and tense. If they differ in pronouns, check the antecedent. If they differ in word order after an introductory phrase, check for a dangling modifier.\nBoundaries: two independent clauses need a period, a semicolon, a colon or comma + and / but / so – never a comma alone. Agreement: find the true subject (ignore phrases between subject and verb). Pronouns: singular nouns and organizations → it / its. Tense: stay consistent unless the time changes. Modifiers: the noun after an introductory phrase must be its doer. Possessives: singular 's, plural s', its without an apostrophe.\nNon-restrictive elements need a pair of matching commas or dashes; restrictive ones need none. Don't put a comma between a subject and its verb or before a that-clause. Comparisons must be logical (that of / those of); series must be parallel. Finally, re-read the whole sentence with your choice: the correct answer usually sounds clear, concise and complete.\noptions differ in punctuation → boundaries / non-restrictive elements / unnecessary commas\noptions differ in verbs → agreement and tense\noptions differ in pronouns or word order → antecedents and modifiers\nalways re-read the whole sentence with your answer","examples":["Al-Qarawiyyin was founded in 859; it is still open today. (boundary)","The collection of rare manuscripts is kept in a special room. (agreement)","The university changed its admission policy. (pronoun)","Having studied in Fez, the scholar returned to teach in Andalusia. (modifier)","The scholars' notes were published together. (possessive)","Ibn Sina, who wrote the \"Canon of Medicine\", was born near Bukhara. (non-restrictive)","The influence of al-Khwarizmi is greater than that of any other mathematician of his age. (comparison)","She founded a school, trained teachers and wrote textbooks. (parallelism)"],"common_errors":["✗ The university was founded in 859, it is still open today. → ✓ The university was founded in 859; it is still open today. (Comma splice.)","✗ The collection of manuscripts are kept in a special room. → ✓ The collection of manuscripts is kept in a special room. (Subject = collection.)","✗ Having studied in Fez, the university welcomed him as a teacher. → ✓ Having studied in Fez, he was welcomed by the university as a teacher. (Dangling modifier.)","✗ The library changed it's opening hours. → ✓ The library changed its opening hours. (its (possessive).)"],"arabic":"أسئلة القواعد في SAT تختبر مجموعة محدودة من المهارات، والخطوة الأولى: انظر كيف تختلف الخيارات.\nإذا اختلفت في الترقيم فالسؤال عن الحدود أو العناصر غير المقيِّدة أو الفواصل الزائدة، وإذا اختلفت في الأفعال فهو عن الاتفاق والزمن، وإذا اختلفت في الضمائر أو الترتيب فهو عن المرجع والمعدِّلات.\nالحدود: جملتان مستقلتان تحتاجان نقطة أو فاصلة منقوطة أو نقطتين أو فاصلة مع أداة عطف، والاتفاق مع الفاعل الحقيقي، والمؤسسات تأخذ its.\nالمقارنات منطقية والسلاسل متوازية، ثم نعيد قراءة الجملة كاملة مع الإجابة المختارة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Final Edit: Comprehensive Conventions Review (SAT)”. Let’s learn mixed review of Standard English conventions: sentence boundaries (comma splices, run-ons, fragments, semicolons, colons, dashes); subject–verb and pronoun–antecedent agreement; verb tense and aspect consistency; modifier placement and dangling modifiers; possessives and plurals; punctuation of non-restrictive elements and appositives; unnecessary commas; logical comparisons; parallel structure together.","on_screen":"GV-L12-U6-LS4 | The Final Edit: Comprehensive Conventions Review (SAT)","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"SAT conventions questions test a small set of skills again and again. Step 1: look at how the options differ. If they differ in punctuation, it is a boundary or punctuation question. If they differ in verb forms, check agreement and tense. If they differ in pronouns, check the antecedent. If they differ in word order after an introductory phrase, check for a dangling modifier.","on_screen":"mixed review of Standard English conventions: sentence boundaries (comma splices, run-ons, fragments, semicolons, colons, dashes); subject–verb and pronoun–antecedent agreement; verb tense and aspect consistency; modifier placement and dangling modifiers; possessives and plurals; punctuation of non-restrictive elements and appositives; unnecessary commas; logical comparisons; parallel structure","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"SAT conventions questions test a small set of skills again and again. Step 1: look at how the options differ. If they differ in punctuation, it is a boundary or punctuation question. If they differ in verb forms, check agreement and tense. If they differ in pronouns, check the antecedent. If they differ in word order after an introductory phrase, check for a dangling modifier. Boundaries: two independent clauses need a period, a semicolon, a colon or comma + and / but / so – never a comma alone. Agreement: find the true subject (ignore phrases between subject and verb). Pronouns: singular nouns and organizations → it / its. Tense: stay consistent unless the time changes. Modifiers: the noun after an introductory phrase must be its doer. Possessives: singular 's, plural s', its without an apostrophe.","on_screen":"options differ in punctuation → boundaries / non-restrictive elements / unnecessary commas • options differ in verbs → agreement and tense • options differ in pronouns or word order → antecedents and modifiers","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Al-Qarawiyyin was founded in 859; it is still open today. (boundary) The collection of rare manuscripts is kept in a special room. (agreement) The university changed its admission policy. (pronoun)","on_screen":"Al-Qarawiyyin was founded in 859; it is still open today. (boundary) / The collection of rare manuscripts is kept in a special room. (agreement) / The university changed its admission policy. (pronoun)","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The university was founded in 859, it is still open today.” That’s not right. We say: “The university was founded in 859; it is still open today.” Comma splice.","on_screen":"✗ The university was founded in 859, it is still open today.   ✓ The university was founded in 859; it is still open today.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:15","narration":"Quick check: The options differ only in punctuation. What kind of question is it? … Think! … A boundary or punctuation question. Great job! Now you can say: I can identify which convention an SAT question is testing before I answer it.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can identify which convention an SAT question is testing before I answer it.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: mixed review of Standard English conventions: sentence boundaries (comma splices, run-ons, fragments, semicolons, colons, dashes); subject–verb and pronoun–antecedent agreement; verb tense and aspect consistency; modifier placement and dangling modifiers; possessives and plurals; punctuation of non-restrictive elements and appositives; unnecessary commas; logical comparisons; parallel structure.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","أسئلة القواعد في SAT تختبر مجموعة محدودة من المهارات، والخطوة الأولى: انظر كيف تختلف الخيارات.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The university was founded in 859, it is still open today. — الصحيح: The university was founded in 859; it is still open today.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أحدد القاعدة التي يختبرها سؤال SAT قبل أن أجيب."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"A Pioneer of Learning (editing passage)","body":"Fatima al-Fihri was born in Kairouan in the early ninth century, her family later moved to Fez. After her father died, she and her sister inherited there father's fortune. In 859, she founded a mosque and a school that has educated students for more than eleven centuries. Today, the university's libraries collection includes rare manuscripts. Her legacy is greater than any other founder of her era.","word_count":66,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the answer that conforms to the conventions of Standard English.","items":[{"q":"Al-Qarawiyyin was founded in the city of Fez in ______ it is still teaching students more than eleven centuries later.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["859","859, and,","859,","859;"],"answer":"859;","explanation":"Sentence boundaries.","explanation_ar":"حدود الجمل."},{"q":"The collection of rare manuscripts donated by the scholar's family ______ kept in a climate-controlled room on the library's top floor.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["is","were","have been","are"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Subject–verb or pronoun agreement.","explanation_ar":"الاتفاق."},{"q":"Having studied mathematics in Baghdad for many ______ wrote a book that would shape the subject for centuries.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["years; al-Khwarizmi","years, al-Khwarizmi","years, a book was written by al-Khwarizmi that","years al-Khwarizmi,"],"answer":"years, al-Khwarizmi","explanation":"Modifier placement.","explanation_ar":"المعدِّلات."},{"q":"The university announced that ______ library would be open to the public every Friday afternoon.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["their","its","they're","it's"],"answer":"its","explanation":"Possessives and plurals.","explanation_ar":"الملكية والجمع."},{"q":"Ibn ______ was born near Bukhara in 980.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["Sina – who wrote the \"Canon of Medicine,\"","Sina, who wrote the \"Canon of Medicine\"","Sina who wrote the \"Canon of Medicine,\"","Sina, who wrote the \"Canon of Medicine,\""],"answer":"Sina, who wrote the \"Canon of Medicine,\"","explanation":"Non-restrictive elements and unnecessary commas.","explanation_ar":"العناصر غير المقيِّدة."},{"q":"Many historians believe that the influence of al-Khwarizmi on modern mathematics is greater than ______ any other scholar of the ninth century.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["it of","that","that of","those of"],"answer":"that of","explanation":"Logical comparisons and parallelism.","explanation_ar":"المقارنة والتوازي."}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the error.","items":[{"q":"The two scholar's notebooks were published together.","options":[],"answer":"The two scholars' notebooks were published together.","explanation":"scholar's → scholars'. Possessives and plurals.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: scholar's → scholars'. الملكية والجمع."},{"q":"The founder of the library believe that books should be free for everyone.","options":[],"answer":"The founder of the library believes that books should be free for everyone.","explanation":"believe → believes. Subject–verb or pronoun agreement.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: believe → believes. الاتفاق."},{"q":"The building was restored in 2010, it is now a museum.","options":[],"answer":"The building was restored in 2010; it is now a museum.","explanation":"2010, it → 2010; it. Sentence boundaries.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: 2010, it → 2010; it. حدود الجمل."}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS4-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the error.","items":[{"q":"She founded a school, trained teachers and was writing textbooks.","options":[],"answer":"She founded a school, trained teachers and wrote textbooks.","explanation":"was writing → wrote. Logical comparisons and parallelism.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: was writing → wrote. المقارنة والتوازي."},{"q":"My brother, Saad, is studying in Riyadh. (I have three brothers.)","options":[],"answer":"My brother Saad is studying in Riyadh. (I have three brothers.)","explanation":"My brother, Saad, is → My brother Saad is. Non-restrictive elements and unnecessary commas.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: My brother, Saad, is → My brother Saad is. العناصر غير المقيِّدة."},{"q":"Walking through the old library, the smell of old paper surprised me.","options":[],"answer":"Walking through the old library, I was surprised by the smell of old paper.","explanation":"Walking through the old library, the smell of old paper surprised me → Walking through the old library, I was surprised by the smell of old paper. Modifier placement.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Walking through the old library, the smell of old paper surprised me → Walking through the old library, I was surprised by the smell of old paper. المعدِّلات."}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the biography.","items":[{"q":"Fatima al-Fihri was born in Kairouan in the early ninth century, her family later moved to Fez.","options":[],"answer":"Fatima al-Fihri was born in Kairouan in the early ninth century; her family later moved to Fez.","explanation":"century, her → century; her. Sentence boundaries.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: century, her → century; her. حدود الجمل."},{"q":"After her father died, she and her sister inherited there father's fortune.","options":[],"answer":"After her father died, she and her sister inherited their father's fortune.","explanation":"there → their. Sentence boundaries.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: there → their. حدود الجمل."},{"q":"In 859, she founded a mosque and a school that has educated students for more than eleven centuries.","options":[],"answer":"In 859, she founded a mosque and a school that have educated students for more than eleven centuries.","explanation":"has → have. Sentence boundaries.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: has → have. حدود الجمل."},{"q":"Today, the university's libraries collection includes rare manuscripts.","options":[],"answer":"Today, the university's library collection includes rare manuscripts.","explanation":"libraries → library. Sentence boundaries.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: libraries → library. حدود الجمل."},{"q":"Her legacy is greater than any other founder of her era.","options":[],"answer":"Her legacy is greater than that of any other founder of her era.","explanation":"any other founder → that of any other founder. Sentence boundaries.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: any other founder → that of any other founder. حدود الجمل."}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write correctly.","items":[{"q":"Write a sentence joining two independent clauses with a semicolon.","options":[],"answer":"The library opened in 1975; it now holds thousands of manuscripts.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mixed review of Standard English conventions: sentence boundaries (comma splices, run-ons, fragments, semicolons, colons, dashes); subject–verb and pronoun–antecedent agreement; verb tense and aspect consistency; modifier placement and dangling modifiers; possessives and plurals; punctuation of non-restrictive elements and appositives; unnecessary commas; logical comparisons; parallel structure correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with an introductory participle phrase and the correct subject.","options":[],"answer":"Having read the scholar's biography, I understood why he is so respected.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mixed review of Standard English conventions: sentence boundaries (comma splices, run-ons, fragments, semicolons, colons, dashes); subject–verb and pronoun–antecedent agreement; verb tense and aspect consistency; modifier placement and dangling modifiers; possessives and plurals; punctuation of non-restrictive elements and appositives; unnecessary commas; logical comparisons; parallel structure correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with a non-restrictive clause punctuated with commas.","options":[],"answer":"Ibn Battuta, who traveled for nearly thirty years, wrote a famous account of his journeys.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mixed review of Standard English conventions: sentence boundaries (comma splices, run-ons, fragments, semicolons, colons, dashes); subject–verb and pronoun–antecedent agreement; verb tense and aspect consistency; modifier placement and dangling modifiers; possessives and plurals; punctuation of non-restrictive elements and appositives; unnecessary commas; logical comparisons; parallel structure correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Letter Ladder","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["The leader chooses a word from the list and draws one blank line per letter.","Teams take turns guessing letters. Correct letters are written on the lines.","Each wrong guess removes one rung of the ladder (start with 6 rungs).","The team that completes the word scores 2 points and uses it in a sentence."],"data":[{"word":"pioneer","clue":"one of the first people to do something new"},{"word":"posterity","clue":"all the people who will live in the future"},{"word":"posthumous","clue":"happening after a person's death"},{"word":"commemorate","clue":"to remember and honor an important person or event"},{"word":"perpetuate","clue":"to make something continue for a long time"},{"word":"heirloom","clue":"a valuable object passed down through a family"},{"word":"enduring","clue":"lasting for a long time"},{"word":"trailblazer","clue":"a person who is the first to do something and shows others the way"},{"word":"bequeath","clue":"to leave property or ideas to others after you die"},{"word":"testament","clue":"something that clearly shows that something is true or exists"},{"word":"immortalize","clue":"to make someone or something remembered forever"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["The museum, which opened in 2019 attracts thousands of visitors.","The museum, which opened in 2019, attracts thousands of visitors.","The museum; which opened in 2019, attracts thousands of visitors.","The museum which opened in 2019, attracts thousands of visitors."],"answer":"The museum, which opened in 2019, attracts thousands of visitors.","explanation":"Non-restrictive elements and unnecessary commas.","explanation_ar":"العناصر غير المقيِّدة."},{"q":"","options":["Each of the scholars are writing a book about the city.","Each of the scholars has written a book about the city.","Each of the scholars have written a book about the city.","Each of the scholars were writing a book about the city."],"answer":"Each of the scholars has written a book about the city.","explanation":"Subject–verb or pronoun agreement.","explanation_ar":"الاتفاق."},{"q":"","options":["The scholar returned home in 1150, and, he had been away for twenty years.","The scholar returned home in 1150 he had been away for twenty years.","The scholar returned home in 1150; he had been away for twenty years.","The scholar returned home in 1150, he had been away for twenty years."],"answer":"The scholar returned home in 1150; he had been away for twenty years.","explanation":"Sentence boundaries.","explanation_ar":"حدود الجمل."},{"q":"","options":["The childrens' library was named after the city's first teacher.","The childrens library was named after the city's first teacher.","The children's library was named after the city's first teacher.","The children's library was named after the citys' first teacher."],"answer":"The children's library was named after the city's first teacher.","explanation":"Possessives and plurals.","explanation_ar":"الملكية والجمع."},{"q":"","options":["After reading the old letters, tears came to my grandfather's eyes.","After reading the old letters, it made my grandfather cry.","After reading the old letters, the tears were my grandfather's.","After reading the old letters, my grandfather began to cry."],"answer":"After reading the old letters, my grandfather began to cry.","explanation":"Modifier placement.","explanation_ar":"المعدِّلات."},{"q":"","options":["The festival celebrates poetry, musical and storytelling.","The festival celebrates poetry, music and telling stories, too, it does.","The festival celebrates poetry, music and to tell stories.","The festival celebrates poetry, music and storytelling."],"answer":"The festival celebrates poetry, music and storytelling.","explanation":"Logical comparisons and parallelism.","explanation_ar":"المقارنة والتوازي."},{"q":"Many of the manuscripts in the collection were copied by ______ who worked in the city's great libraries during the twelfth century.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["scribe's","scribes","scribes,","scribes'"],"answer":"scribes","explanation":"Possessives and plurals.","explanation_ar":"الملكية والجمع."},{"q":"The scholars who founded the observatory hoped that ______ work would help future generations understand the movement of the stars.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["its","his","it's","their"],"answer":"their","explanation":"Subject–verb or pronoun agreement.","explanation_ar":"الاتفاق."},{"q":"The ancient trade route connected southern Arabia with the Mediterranean ______ merchants carried frankincense, spices and textiles along it for centuries.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["world;","world, and,","world,","world"],"answer":"world;","explanation":"Sentence boundaries.","explanation_ar":"حدود الجمل."},{"q":"When an SAT question's options differ only in punctuation, what should you check first?","options":["whether the clauses on each side are independent","the length of the options","the meaning of the vocabulary","the spelling of the words"],"answer":"whether the clauses on each side are independent","explanation":"Sentence boundaries.","explanation_ar":"حدود الجمل."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Legacy” that shows mixed review of Standard English conventions: sentence boundaries (comma splices, run-ons, fragments, semicolons, colons, dashes); subject–verb and pronoun–antecedent agreement; verb tense and aspect consistency; modifier placement and dangling modifiers; possessives and plurals; punctuation of non-restrictive elements and appositives; unnecessary commas; logical comparisons; parallel structure in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Legacy” that shows mixed review of Standard English conventions: sentence boundaries (comma splices, run-ons, fragments, semicolons, colons, dashes); subject–verb and pronoun–antecedent agreement; verb tense and aspect consistency; modifier placement and dangling modifiers; possessives and plurals; punctuation of non-restrictive elements and appositives; unnecessary commas; logical comparisons; parallel structure in action"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Letter Ladder”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Letter Ladder"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Final Edit: Comprehensive Conventions Review (SAT)”. Let’s learn mixed review of Standard English conventions: sentence boundaries (comma splices, run-ons, fragments, semicolons, colons, dashes); subject–verb and pronoun–antecedent agreement; verb tense and aspect consistency; modifier placement and dangling modifiers; possessives and plurals; punctuation of non-restrictive elements and appositives; unnecessary commas; logical comparisons; parallel structure together. SAT conventions questions test a small set of skills again and again. Step 1: look at how the options differ. If they differ in punctuation, it is a boundary or punctuation question. If they differ in verb forms, check agreement and tense. If they differ in pronouns, check the antecedent. If they differ in word order after an introductory phrase, check for a dangling modifier. SAT conventions questions test a small set of skills again and again. Step 1: look at how the options differ. If they differ in punctuation, it is a boundary or punctuation question. If they differ in verb forms, check agreement and tense. If they differ in pronouns, check the antecedent. If they differ in word order after an introductory phrase, check for a dangling modifier. Boundaries: two independent clauses need a period, a semicolon, a colon or comma + and / but / so – never a comma alone. Agreement: find the true subject (ignore phrases between subject and verb). Pronouns: singular nouns and organizations → it / its. Tense: stay consistent unless the time changes. Modifiers: the noun after an introductory phrase must be its doer. Possessives: singular 's, plural s', its without an apostrophe. Here are some examples. Al-Qarawiyyin was founded in 859; it is still open today. (boundary) The collection of rare manuscripts is kept in a special room. (agreement) The university changed its admission policy. (pronoun) Be careful! Some learners say: “The university was founded in 859, it is still open today.” That’s not right. We say: “The university was founded in 859; it is still open today.” Comma splice. Quick check: The options differ only in punctuation. What kind of question is it? … Think! … A boundary or punctuation question. Great job! Now you can say: I can identify which convention an SAT question is testing before I answer it.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.05"}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS5","title":"The Legacy I Want to Leave: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to deliver a reflective speech about the legacy they hope to leave.","Students will be able to write a polished reflective essay that draws on the full range of advanced grammar and vocabulary, and answer SAT-style transition and synthesis items.","I can give a reflective speech about the legacy I want to leave.","I can write a polished, stylish reflective essay."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من إلقاء كلمة تأملية عن الإرث الذي يأملون أن يتركوه.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة مقال تأملي متقن يستفيد من كامل القواعد والمفردات المتقدمة، والإجابة عن أسئلة الروابط والتركيب بنمط SAT.","أستطيع أن ألقي كلمة تأملية عن الإرث الذي أريد أن أتركه.","أستطيع أن أكتب مقالًا تأمليًّا متقنًا وأنيقًا."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"pioneer","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌpaɪəˈnɪr/","definition":"one of the first people to do something new","arabic":"رائد","example":"Ibn Sina was a pioneer of modern medicine.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"enduring","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ɛndˈjʊrɪŋ/","definition":"lasting for a long time","arabic":"دائم / باقٍ","example":"Her poems have had an enduring influence.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"trailblazer","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtreɪlˌbleɪzɚ/","definition":"a person who is the first to do something and shows others the way","arabic":"رائد يشقّ الطريق","example":"She was a trailblazer for women in science.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"posterity","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pɑˈstɛrəti/","definition":"all the people who will live in the future","arabic":"الأجيال القادمة","example":"The letters were preserved for posterity.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"posthumous","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈpɑstʃʊməs/","definition":"happening after a person's death","arabic":"بعد الوفاة","example":"The novel was a posthumous success.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"commemorate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kəˈmɛmɚˌeɪt/","definition":"to remember and honor an important person or event","arabic":"يُحيي ذكرى","example":"A statue commemorates the city's founder.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"perpetuate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/pɚˈpɛtʃəˌweɪt/","definition":"to make something continue for a long time","arabic":"يُديم / يُخلّد","example":"The festival perpetuates an ancient tradition.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"bequeath","pos":"verb","ipa":"/bɪˈkwiθ/","definition":"to leave property or ideas to others after you die","arabic":"يورّث / يوصي بـ","example":"He bequeathed his library to the university.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"testament","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtɛstəmənt/","definition":"something that clearly shows that something is true or exists","arabic":"شاهد / دليل","example":"The mosque is a testament to the skill of its builders.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"immortalize","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˌɪˈmɔrtəlaɪz/","definition":"to make someone or something remembered forever","arabic":"يخلّد","example":"The poet immortalized his hometown in verse.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"seminal","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈsɛmənəl/","definition":"very important and influencing later developments","arabic":"رائد / مؤسِّس","example":"It was a seminal work in the history of mathematics.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"monumental","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌmɑnjəˈmɛntəl/","definition":"very large, important or impressive","arabic":"ضخم / عظيم الأثر","example":"Building the canal was a monumental achievement.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"revere","pos":"verb","ipa":"/rɪˈvɪr/","definition":"to respect and admire someone deeply","arabic":"يُجلّ / يوقّر","example":"The scholar is revered across the Arab world.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"endowment","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɛnˈdaʊmənt/","definition":"money given to an institution to provide a regular income","arabic":"وقف / منحة دائمة","example":"The university's endowment funds hundreds of scholarships.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"heirloom","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɛrˌlum/","definition":"a valuable object passed down through a family","arabic":"إرث عائلي / تحفة متوارثة","example":"This silver coffee pot is a family heirloom.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 6 – and, in fact, the whole strand: tense and aspect for stance, grammar for style, legacy vocabulary and comprehensive conventions.\nA polished reflective essay opens with a specific memory or image, shows how a person or experience has shaped you (present perfect), emphasizes key ideas with cleft sentences or inversion, combines ideas elegantly with participle phrases and appositives, and ends with a forward-looking commitment. Check every sentence for conventions before you finish.\n✔ opened (1975) • has been lending • will have left\n✔ It was in that bookshop that… • Never did he ask…\n✔ His shelves now nearly empty, … • Having studied…, I…\n✔ pass the torch • follow in their footsteps • pave the way • leave a legacy","examples":["In 1975, my grandfather opened a small bookshop.","He has been lending books to students for almost fifty years.","It was in that bookshop that I first fell in love with reading.","Never did he ask for anything in return.","His shelves now nearly empty, he passed the torch to my father.","I hope to follow in their footsteps.","Having studied computer science, I want to build a free online library.","I will have left a legacy worth remembering."],"common_errors":["✗ In 1975, my grandfather has opened a bookshop. → ✓ In 1975, my grandfather opened a bookshop. (Finished time → past simple.)","✗ Never he asked for anything in return. → ✓ Never did he ask for anything in return. (Inversion.)","✗ Having studied computer science, a free library is my dream. → ✓ Having studied computer science, I dream of building a free library. (Dangling modifier.)"],"arabic":"نراجع الزمن والجهة للتعبير عن الموقف، والقواعد لأغراض أسلوبية، ومفردات الإرث، وجميع القواعد الكتابية – بل نراجع المسار كله.\nالمقال التأملي المتقن يبدأ بذكرى محددة، ويُظهر كيف شكّلك شخص أو تجربة (المضارع التام)، ويؤكد الأفكار الرئيسة بالجمل المشطورة أو القلب، ويدمج الأفكار بعبارات اسم الفاعل والبدل، وينتهي بالتزام نحو المستقبل.\nراجع كل جملة من حيث القواعد الكتابية قبل أن تنتهي."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Legacy I Want to Leave: Language in Use”. Let’s learn tense and aspect for stance, grammar for style, legacy vocabulary and idioms, comprehensive conventions; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (final review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L12-U6-LS5 | The Legacy I Want to Leave: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Graduation reflections: prepare a 2-minute speech about the legacy you hope to leave. Include one present perfect continuous sentence about someone who has influenced you, one cleft sentence, one fronted or inverted sentence, three legacy idioms or words, and one sentence that combines several ideas with a participle phrase or appositive.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 6 – and, in fact, the whole strand: tense and aspect for stance, grammar for style, legacy vocabulary and comprehensive conventions. A polished reflective essay opens with a specific memory or image, shows how a person or experience has shaped you (present perfect), emphasizes key ideas with cleft sentences or inversion, combines ideas elegantly with participle phrases and appositives, and ends with a forward-looking commitment. Check every sentence for conventions before you finish.","on_screen":"✔ opened (1975) • has been lending • will have left • ✔ It was in that bookshop that… • Never did he ask… • ✔ His shelves now nearly empty, … • Having studied…, I…","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. In 1975, my grandfather opened a small bookshop. He has been lending books to students for almost fifty years. It was in that bookshop that I first fell in love with reading.","on_screen":"In 1975, my grandfather opened a small bookshop. / He has been lending books to students for almost fifty years. / It was in that bookshop that I first fell in love with reading.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “In 1975, my grandfather has opened a bookshop.” That’s not right. We say: “In 1975, my grandfather opened a bookshop.” Finished time → past simple.","on_screen":"✗ In 1975, my grandfather has opened a bookshop.   ✓ In 1975, my grandfather opened a bookshop.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:15","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “Never he asked for anything in return.”? … Think! … It should be “Never did he ask for anything in return.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can give a reflective speech about the legacy I want to leave.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can give a reflective speech about the legacy I want to leave.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: tense and aspect for stance, grammar for style, legacy vocabulary and idioms, comprehensive conventions; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (final review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع الزمن والجهة للتعبير عن الموقف، والقواعد لأغراض أسلوبية، ومفردات الإرث، وجميع القواعد الكتابية – بل نراجع المسار كله.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: In 1975, my grandfather has opened a bookshop. — الصحيح: In 1975, my grandfather opened a bookshop.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن ألقي كلمة تأملية عن الإرث الذي أريد أن أتركه."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"The Legacy I Want to Leave – Omar","body":"In 1975, my grandfather opened a small bookshop in the old market of Taif.\nFor almost fifty years, he has been lending books to students who could not afford to buy them.\nIt was in that bookshop that I first fell in love with reading.\nNever did he ask for anything in return; he simply believed that knowledge should be shared.\nHis shelves now nearly empty, my grandfather recently passed the torch to my father.\nI hope to follow in their footsteps, though perhaps in a different way.\nHaving studied computer science, I want to build a free online library for students across the Arab world.\nIf I can pave the way for even one young reader, I will have left a legacy worth remembering.","word_count":125,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Omar's essay. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Omar's grandfather opened a bookshop in Taif in 1975.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Legacy I Want to Leave – Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"His grandfather sold books only to students who could pay.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Legacy I Want to Leave – Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Omar first fell in love with reading in his grandfather's bookshop.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Legacy I Want to Leave – Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"His grandfather always asked for something in return.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Legacy I Want to Leave – Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The bookshop has now been passed to Omar's father.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Legacy I Want to Leave – Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Omar wants to become a bookshop owner in Taif.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Legacy I Want to Leave – Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"In 1975, my grandfather ___ a small bookshop in the old market.","options":["had been opened","has opened","opened","has been opening"],"answer":"opened","explanation":"Tense and aspect for stance.","explanation_ar":"الزمن والجهة."},{"q":"For almost fifty years, he ___ books to students who could not afford them.","options":["lends since","has been lending","lent since","is lending since"],"answer":"has been lending","explanation":"Tense and aspect for stance.","explanation_ar":"الزمن والجهة."},{"q":"___ in that bookshop that I first fell in love with reading.","options":["There was","That was","It is being","It was"],"answer":"It was","explanation":"Grammar for style (cleft, inversion, participle).","explanation_ar":"القواعد للأسلوب."},{"q":"Never ___ for anything in return.","options":["did he ask","he asked","asked he","he did ask"],"answer":"did he ask","explanation":"Grammar for style (cleft, inversion, participle).","explanation_ar":"القواعد للأسلوب."},{"q":"My grandfather recently passed the ___ to my father.","options":["candle","torch","flame","light"],"answer":"torch","explanation":"Legacy vocabulary or idiom.","explanation_ar":"مفردات الإرث."},{"q":"My grandfather lent thousands of books without asking for payment. ______ many of the students he helped became teachers, doctors and engineers.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Over the years,","However,","Nevertheless,","In contrast,"],"answer":"Over the years,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Prepare your graduation speech.","items":[{"q":"A memory with a specific date (past simple): ___","options":[],"answer":"In 2015, my mother started a reading club for the girls in our neighborhood.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses tense and aspect for stance, grammar for style, legacy vocabulary and idioms, comprehensive conventions; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (final review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Someone's ongoing influence (present perfect continuous): ___","options":[],"answer":"Since then, she has been inspiring dozens of young readers.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses tense and aspect for stance, grammar for style, legacy vocabulary and idioms, comprehensive conventions; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (final review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A cleft sentence: ___","options":[],"answer":"It was my mother who taught me that every child deserves books.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses tense and aspect for stance, grammar for style, legacy vocabulary and idioms, comprehensive conventions; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (final review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A fronted or inverted sentence: ___","options":[],"answer":"Rarely have I met anyone as patient as she is.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses tense and aspect for stance, grammar for style, legacy vocabulary and idioms, comprehensive conventions; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (final review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Your commitment with a legacy idiom: ___","options":[],"answer":"I hope to follow in her footsteps and pave the way for others.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses tense and aspect for stance, grammar for style, legacy vocabulary and idioms, comprehensive conventions; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (final review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your reflective essay.","items":[{"q":"Plan: memory, influence, emphasis, your plans, commitment.","options":[],"answer":"Grandmother's garden in Abha; she has been planting trees for forty years; It was in her garden that I learned patience; I want to study agriculture; leave greener land for posterity","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses tense and aspect for stance, grammar for style, legacy vocabulary and idioms, comprehensive conventions; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (final review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your reflective essay \"The Legacy I Want to Leave\" (8–9 sentences).","options":[],"answer":"When I was six, my grandmother gave me a small olive tree to plant in her garden in Abha. For forty years, she has been planting trees on the hillside behind her house. It was in that garden that I learned patience, hard work and respect for the land. Never did she complain about the dry summers or the cold winters. Her hands now too weak to dig, she has passed the torch to me. Having decided to study agriculture, I hope to follow in her footsteps on a larger scale. I want to help farmers in arid regions plant native trees that will stand the test of time. If I succeed, I will have left posterity a greener land than the one I inherited.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses tense and aspect for stance, grammar for style, legacy vocabulary and idioms, comprehensive conventions; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (final review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Final check: past simple vs present perfect? inversion and cleft correct? no dangling modifiers or comma splices? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"Having decided to study agriculture, my dream is\" to \"Having decided to study agriculture, I hope\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses tense and aspect for stance, grammar for style, legacy vocabulary and idioms, comprehensive conventions; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (final review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Treasure Hunt Review","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Teams move to a station every 90 seconds.","At each station, write one correct sentence with the cue word and tense and aspect for stance, grammar for style, legacy vocabulary and idioms, comprehensive conventions; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (final review).","Teams collect a \"treasure letter\" for each correct sentence.","Unscramble the letters at the end to reveal the secret word."],"data":[{"cue":"pioneer","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"enduring","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"trailblazer","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"posterity","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"posthumous","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"commemorate","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"perpetuate","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"bequeath","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"testament","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"immortalize","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"seminal","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"monumental","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"revere","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"endowment","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"heirloom","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The library ___ thousands of students since it opened in 1985.","options":["has served","is serving since","serves since","served since"],"answer":"has served","explanation":"Tense and aspect for stance.","explanation_ar":"الزمن والجهة."},{"q":"___ my teacher who encouraged me to write my first story.","options":["She was it","It was","That was","There was"],"answer":"It was","explanation":"Grammar for style (cleft, inversion, participle).","explanation_ar":"القواعد للأسلوب."},{"q":"___ by generations of readers, her novels have stood the test of time.","options":["Loving","Love","Loved","Having loved"],"answer":"Loved","explanation":"Grammar for style (cleft, inversion, participle).","explanation_ar":"القواعد للأسلوب."},{"q":"The family recorded the old songs for ___.","options":["posterity","endowment","heirloom","testament"],"answer":"posterity","explanation":"Legacy vocabulary or idiom.","explanation_ar":"مفردات الإرث."},{"q":"","options":["The scholar's ideas influenced thinkers since nine centuries.","The scholar's ideas have influenced thinkers since nine centuries.","The scholar's ideas are influencing thinkers for nine centuries.","The scholar's ideas have influenced thinkers for nine centuries."],"answer":"The scholar's ideas have influenced thinkers for nine centuries.","explanation":"Tense and aspect for stance.","explanation_ar":"الزمن والجهة."},{"q":"My grandfather never went to university. ______ he became one of the most respected teachers in the region.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["For example,","Nevertheless,","Therefore,","Similarly,"],"answer":"Nevertheless,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"Al-Khwarizmi's book introduced systematic methods for solving equations. ______ the word \"algebra\" itself comes from its title.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["In fact,","Nevertheless,","In contrast,","However,"],"answer":"In fact,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Fatima al-Fihri founded al-Qarawiyyin in Fez in 859.\n• She used a fortune inherited from her father.\n• The institution has been teaching students for more than eleven centuries.\n• Many regard it as the oldest continuously operating university in the world.\n\nThe student wants to emphasize the enduring nature of al-Fihri's legacy. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Fatima al-Fihri inherited a fortune from her father.","Al-Qarawiyyin is in Fez.","Many universities are old.","Founded by Fatima al-Fihri in 859, al-Qarawiyyin has been teaching students for more than eleven centuries."],"answer":"Founded by Fatima al-Fihri in 859, al-Qarawiyyin has been teaching students for more than eleven centuries.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis.","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Ibn Sina wrote the \"Canon of Medicine\" in the eleventh century.\n• The book organized the medical knowledge of his time.\n• It was studied in European universities for centuries.\n• Historians continue to reassess its influence.\n\nThe student wants to explain the reach of Ibn Sina's influence. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Ibn Sina wrote a book.","Historians continue to reassess its influence.","Ibn Sina's \"Canon of Medicine,\" written in the eleventh century, was studied in European universities for centuries.","Medicine is important."],"answer":"Ibn Sina's \"Canon of Medicine,\" written in the eleventh century, was studied in European universities for centuries.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis.","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."},{"q":"Pick the best concluding sentence for a reflective essay about legacy:","options":["If I can pave the road for even one young reader, I left a legacy worth remembering.","If I can pave the way for even one young reader, I will have left a legacy worth remembering.","If I can pave the way for even one young reader I will have left, a legacy worth remembering.","Having paved the way, a legacy will be left by me, worth remembering."],"answer":"If I can pave the way for even one young reader, I will have left a legacy worth remembering.","explanation":"Legacy vocabulary or idiom.","explanation_ar":"مفردات الإرث."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"A graduation ceremony: Omar at the podium delivering a speech titled \"The Legacy I Want to Leave\"; a photo slideshow behind him showing his grandfather's bookshop, his school years and a young tree he planted; families in the audience. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A graduation ceremony: Omar at the podium delivering a speech titled \"The Legacy I Want to Leave\"; a photo slideshow behind him showing his grandfather's bookshop, his school years and a young tree he planted; families in the audience"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Legacy”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as older teens/young adults aged 16–19, editorial infographic feel. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Legacy”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L12-U6-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Treasure Hunt Review”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Treasure Hunt Review"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS5-T1","script":"In 1975, my grandfather opened a small bookshop in the old market of Taif. For almost fifty years, he has been lending books to students who could not afford to buy them. It was in that bookshop that I first fell in love with reading. Never did he ask for anything in return; he simply believed that knowledge should be shared. His shelves now nearly empty, my grandfather recently passed the torch to my father. I hope to follow in their footsteps, though perhaps in a different way. Having studied computer science, I want to build a free online library for students across the Arab world. If I can pave the way for even one young reader, I will have left a legacy worth remembering.","voice":"en-US, articulate adult voice","speed":"1.05"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L12-U6-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Legacy I Want to Leave: Language in Use”. Let’s learn tense and aspect for stance, grammar for style, legacy vocabulary and idioms, comprehensive conventions; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (final review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Graduation reflections: prepare a 2-minute speech about the legacy you hope to leave. Include one present perfect continuous sentence about someone who has influenced you, one cleft sentence, one fronted or inverted sentence, three legacy idioms or words, and one sentence that combines several ideas with a participle phrase or appositive. Today you use all of Unit 6 – and, in fact, the whole strand: tense and aspect for stance, grammar for style, legacy vocabulary and comprehensive conventions. A polished reflective essay opens with a specific memory or image, shows how a person or experience has shaped you (present perfect), emphasizes key ideas with cleft sentences or inversion, combines ideas elegantly with participle phrases and appositives, and ends with a forward-looking commitment. Check every sentence for conventions before you finish. Here are some examples. In 1975, my grandfather opened a small bookshop. He has been lending books to students for almost fifty years. It was in that bookshop that I first fell in love with reading. Be careful! Some learners say: “In 1975, my grandfather has opened a bookshop.” That’s not right. We say: “In 1975, my grandfather opened a bookshop.” Finished time → past simple. Quick check: what is wrong with “Never he asked for anything in return.”? … Think! … It should be “Never did he ask for anything in return.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can give a reflective speech about the legacy I want to leave.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.05"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"Ibn Battuta ___ his famous journey in 1325.","options":["has begun","began","has been beginning","had begun since"],"answer":"began","explanation":"Past simple vs present perfect (relevance).","explanation_ar":"الماضي أم التام."},{"q":"The university ___ students since the ninth century.","options":["is teaching since","teaches since","taught since","has been teaching"],"answer":"has been teaching","explanation":"Present perfect continuous (duration, ongoing).","explanation_ar":"التام المستمر."},{"q":"By the time she founded the school, she ___ in three countries.","options":["teaches","has taught","had taught","is teaching"],"answer":"had taught","explanation":"Past perfect for background.","explanation_ar":"الماضي التام."},{"q":"Many historians ___ that the Silk Road shaped the cultures of three continents.","options":["argued tomorrow","are argue","argue","have arguing"],"answer":"argue","explanation":"Present simple for the stance of sources.","explanation_ar":"موقف المصادر."},{"q":"You ___ very generous today; usually you keep your sweets to yourself!","options":["are","are being","have been being","be"],"answer":"are being","explanation":"Stative vs dynamic meaning; be being.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال الحالية."},{"q":"Over the past two decades, archaeologists ______ the ancient city of Hegra, revealing new details about the daily lives of the Nabataeans.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["study since","had been studying tomorrow","have been studying","studied since"],"answer":"have been studying","explanation":"Present perfect continuous (duration, ongoing).","explanation_ar":"التام المستمر."},{"q":"___ my grandfather who taught me to play chess.","options":["It was","He was it","There was","That was"],"answer":"It was","explanation":"Cleft sentences for emphasis.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المشطورة."},{"q":"So famous ___ that students traveled from distant countries to hear her lectures.","options":["the scholar did","the scholar was","was the scholar","did the scholar"],"answer":"was the scholar","explanation":"Fronting and inversion for emphasis.","explanation_ar":"التقديم والقلب."},{"q":"The house was built in 1890. It is now a museum. → The house, ___, is now a museum.","options":["which built in 1890","built in 1890","it was built in 1890","building in 1890"],"answer":"built in 1890","explanation":"Combining sentences with advanced structures.","explanation_ar":"دمج الجمل."},{"q":"Which sentence places the most important new information at the end?","options":["The university was founded by a woman named Fatima al-Fihri.","Fatima al-Fihri, by a woman, the university was founded.","A woman founded it, the university, Fatima al-Fihri.","By Fatima al-Fihri, a woman, founded was the university."],"answer":"The university was founded by a woman named Fatima al-Fihri.","explanation":"End focus and concision.","explanation_ar":"التركيز الختامي والإيجاز."},{"q":"The scientist recorded her observations every night. She did this for forty years. Her notebooks are now in a museum.\n\nWhich choice most effectively combines the three sentences?","options":["The notebooks in which the scientist recorded her observations every night for forty years are now in a museum.","For forty years every night the scientist's notebooks recorded, now in a museum.","The scientist, she recorded her observations, which are notebooks, in a museum for forty years.","The scientist recorded observations, and she did this for forty years, and her notebooks are now in a museum."],"answer":"The notebooks in which the scientist recorded her observations every night for forty years are now in a museum.","explanation":"Combining sentences with advanced structures.","explanation_ar":"دمج الجمل."},{"q":"She ___ the way for women in science in her country.","options":["laid down","built","made up","paved"],"answer":"paved","explanation":"Legacy idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"His novels have stood the test of ___.","options":["times","timing","the time","time"],"answer":"time","explanation":"Legacy idiom.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"A statue in the square ___ the city's founder.","options":["perpetuates of","commemorates","bequeaths","reveres to"],"answer":"commemorates","explanation":"Legacy word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Historians consider the ninth-century treatise a ______ work because it introduced methods that mathematicians would build on for the next thousand years.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["posthumous","heirloom","seminal","reverent"],"answer":"seminal","explanation":"Words in context (SAT style).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات في السياق."},{"q":"The old silver coffee pot has been passed down for five generations; it is a treasured family ___.","options":["heirloom","posterity","endowment","testament"],"answer":"heirloom","explanation":"Legacy word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"","options":["The observatory was founded in 1259, and, it attracted astronomers from many lands.","The observatory was founded in 1259; it attracted astronomers from many lands.","The observatory was founded in 1259 it attracted astronomers from many lands.","The observatory was founded in 1259, it attracted astronomers from many lands."],"answer":"The observatory was founded in 1259; it attracted astronomers from many lands.","explanation":"Sentence boundaries.","explanation_ar":"حدود الجمل."},{"q":"","options":["The collection of letters were kept in the national archive.","The collection of letters have been kept in the national archive.","The collection of letters are kept in the national archive.","The collection of letters is kept in the national archive."],"answer":"The collection of letters is kept in the national archive.","explanation":"Subject–verb or pronoun agreement.","explanation_ar":"الاتفاق."},{"q":"Having traveled for nearly thirty ______ dictated an account of his journeys that is still read today.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["years, an account was dictated by Ibn Battuta that","years; Ibn Battuta","years Ibn Battuta,","years, Ibn Battuta"],"answer":"years, Ibn Battuta","explanation":"Modifier placement.","explanation_ar":"المعدِّلات."},{"q":"The library's influence on scholarship in the region was greater than ______ any other institution of its time.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["those of","that of","that","it of"],"answer":"that of","explanation":"Logical comparisons and parallelism.","explanation_ar":"المقارنة والتوازي."},{"q":"Many people assume that great legacies require great wealth. ______ some of the most enduring legacies have been left by teachers, parents and volunteers.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Similarly,","Therefore,","In fact,","For this reason,"],"answer":"In fact,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Al-Khwarizmi was a ninth-century mathematician in Baghdad.\n• The word \"algebra\" comes from the title of his book.\n• The word \"algorithm\" comes from his name.\n• Algorithms are used in all modern computers.\n\nThe student wants to show how al-Khwarizmi's legacy continues today. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["The word \"algorithm,\" derived from al-Khwarizmi's name, describes processes that are used in every modern computer.","The word \"algebra\" comes from a book title.","Mathematicians lived in the ninth century.","Al-Khwarizmi lived in Baghdad."],"answer":"The word \"algorithm,\" derived from al-Khwarizmi's name, describes processes that are used in every modern computer.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis.","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"it was my teachers which inspired me, they has paved the way for my success.\"","options":["it was my teachers who inspired me; they have paved the way for my success.","It was my teachers who inspired me, they have paved the way for my success.","It was my teachers which inspired me; they have paved the way for my success.","It was my teachers who inspired me; they have paved the way for my success."],"answer":"It was my teachers who inspired me; they have paved the way for my success.","explanation":"Cleft sentences for emphasis.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المشطورة."},{"q":"\"Ibn Sina has shaped medicine for centuries.\" What does the present perfect suggest?","options":["His influence continues today.","The sentence is about the future.","He is still alive.","His influence ended long ago."],"answer":"His influence continues today.","explanation":"Past simple vs present perfect (relevance).","explanation_ar":"الماضي أم التام."}],"theme_ar":"الإرث","essential_question_ar":"ماذا سنترك للأجيال التي تأتي بعدنا؟","can_do":"I can choose tense and aspect to express stance and relevance (has shaped vs shaped; has been teaching; is being modest), combine and vary sentences using the full range of advanced grammar for style, use legacy idioms and collocations, and edit a text for all major conventions of Standard English.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أختار الزمن والجهة للتعبير عن الموقف والصلة بالحاضر (has shaped أم shaped / has been teaching / is being modest)، وأدمج الجمل وأنوّعها باستخدام مجموعة القواعد المتقدمة كلها لأغراض أسلوبية، وأستخدم تعابير الإرث ومتلازماته، وأحرّر النص وفق جميع قواعد الإنجليزية المعيارية الرئيسة."});
